t["npc:thyn-tel-bladeweaver"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,360,20.435.0,23.436.1,28.202.0,38.130.0,44.186.0,42.209.0,32.177.0,49.132.0",["h"]="2885d7",["n"]="Thyn'tel Tejespada",["s"]="Thyn'tel Tejespada. Thyn'tel Tejespada es una centinela elfa de la noche apostada en el Bancal del Guerrero en Darnassus. Está profundamente preocupada por la desaparición de la sacerdotisa Velinde Cantoestelar y envía a aventureros de confianza de la Alianza a rastrear pistas sobre su paradero. A través de sus indagaciones, busca recomponer el misterio que se oculta tras la Guadaña de Elune. Montando guardia sobre Darnassus desde el Bancal del Guerrero, Thyn'tel Tejespada representa el brazo militar vigilante de los kaldorei. Cuando la sacerdotisa Velinde Cantoestelar desapareció misteriosamente sin dejar rastro, Thyn'tel se negó a dejar que la pista se enfriara. Intuyendo que fuerzas funestas estaban involucradas, se encarga de encargar a aventureros dispuestos que investiguen las pertenencias personales de la sacerdotisa y descubran adónde la llevó su viaje.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Positioned right among the trainers on the Warrior's Terrace, Thyn'tel is a familiar sentinel face to Alliance warriors passing through Darnassus.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance heroes who visit the Warrior's Terrace are entrusted by Thyn'tel to venture deep into neutral and contested territory to uncover the truth.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Thyn'tel's assignment strikes close to home, uncovering the hidden tragedy of a revered priestess who fell victim to forces beyond her control."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Thyn'tel Bladeweaver is a night elf sentinel located on the Warrior's Terrace in Darnassus. She serves as a quest giver initiating the investigation into the disappearance of Priestess Velinde Starsong.",["al"]={"thyntel bladeweaver","who is thyntel","thyn'tel info"},["q"]="Who is Thyn'tel Bladeweaver?"},{["a"]="She can be found standing in Darnassus, specifically stationed on the Warrior's Terrace among the kaldorei warriors and sentinels.",["al"]={"thyn'tel location","where is thyn'tel bladeweaver","thyntel map"},["q"]="Where can I find Thyn'tel Bladeweaver?"},{["a"]="She is the primary contact for the quest chain investigating Velinde Starsong, providing quests such as 'Velinde's Effects', 'The Barrens Port', and concluding with 'Answered Questions'.",["al"]={"thyntel quests","what quest does she give"},["q"]="What quests does Thyn'tel Bladeweaver offer?"},{["a"]="Velinde Starsong was a priestess who served in Ashenvale until she disappeared abruptly, leaving her work unfinished. Thyn'tel seeks to discover her fate and uncover the dark mystery surrounding her departure.",["al"]={"why investigate velinde","what happened to velinde"},["q"]="Why is she interested in Velinde Starsong?"},{["a"]="After examining Velinde's effects in Darnassus, Thyn'tel directs investigators south across the sea to Ratchet in the Barrens to track down shipping records of Velinde's voyage.",["al"]={"velinde quest path","where does the quest go"},["q"]="Where does her quest chain lead?"},{["a"]="Yes. Stationed within the night elf capital of Darnassus, Thyn'tel Bladeweaver offers quests exclusively to members of the Alliance.",["al"]={"can horde talk to thyntel","is she alliance"},["q"]="Is Thyn'tel Bladeweaver an Alliance-only contact?"}},["kw"]={"bladeweaver","darnassus","scythe of elune","sentinel","starsong","thyn'tel","velinde","warrior's terrace"},["n"]="Thyn'tel Bladeweaver",["s"]="Thyn'tel Bladeweaver is a night elf sentinel stationed at the Warrior's Terrace in Darnassus. She is deeply troubled by the disappearance of Priestess Velinde Starsong and dispatches trusted Alliance adventurers to track down clues regarding her whereabouts. Through her inquiries, she seeks to piece together the unraveling mystery behind the Scythe of Elune.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing watch over Darnassus from the Warrior's Terrace, Thyn'tel Bladeweaver represents the vigilant military arm of the kaldorei. When Priestess Velinde Starsong mysteriously vanished without leaving word, Thyn'tel refused to let the trail go cold. Sensing that grave forces were involved, she takes it upon herself to commission adventurers willing to dig into the priestess's personal belongings and uncover where her journey led.",["t"]="A Sentinel's Inquest"},{["b"]="Thyn'tel directs investigators to inspect Velinde's remaining effects left behind in the capital. The clues uncovered reveal a journal describing Velinde's communion with Elune and the terrifying worgen beasts summoned through the Scythe of Elune. Guided by Thyn'tel, travelers follow the trail southward through the port of Ratchet into the Barrens, attempting to find where the desperate priestess sailed before she vanished entirely.",["t"]="Tracing Velinde's Steps"}}}}}
t["npc:tiza-battleforge"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,411,25.594.0,22.569.1,24.240.0,34.126.0,51.237.0,57.292.0,45.170.0,45.265.0",["h"]="a18f1a",["n"]="Tiza Forjabatalla",["s"]="Tiza Forjabatalla. Tiza Forjabatalla es una veterana paladín enana de los Caballeros de la Mano de Plata destinada en la Sala de los Misterios de Forjaz. Célebre por su firme devoción y perspicacia, guía a los jóvenes paladines enanos por la senda de la virtud, la caridad y la abnegación. A través del estudio de los textos sagrados y de pruebas sobre el terreno, evalúa si los iniciados están verdaderamente preparados para blandir el don de la resurrección de la Luz. En las serenas cámaras de la Sala de los Misterios de Forjaz, Tiza Forjabatalla destaca como una de las paladines enanas más respetadas de los Caballeros de la Mano de Plata. Los iniciados de toda la Alianza —enviados por tutores como Brandur Martiyerro en Forjaz, Azar Martillopujante en Dun Morogh y Lord Grisillo Quiebrasombras en Ventormenta— acuden a ella para avanzar en su instrucción espiritual. Tiza sostiene que la Luz Sagrada exige más que destreza marcial; requiere un servicio humilde, compasión y una entereza inquebrantable frente a la oscuridad invasora de la Plaga y otras amenazas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="For dwarven paladins, Tiza Battleforge is a pivotal mentor who tests your worthiness through the Tome of Divinity and entrusts you with the power to resurrect fallen allies.",["faction:Alliance"]="Working closely with mentors from Stormwind to Kharanos, Tiza ensures the Silver Hand maintains unified standards of virtue and martial readiness across all Alliance lands.",["race:Dwarf"]="Tiza represents the deep integration of the Holy Light within dwarven culture and the Silver Hand, guiding Khaz Modan's defenders against threats like the Dark Iron clan."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Tiza Battleforge is an esteemed dwarven paladin belonging to the Knights of the Silver Hand. Located in the Hall of Mysteries within Ironforge, she tests and mentors dwarven paladins who are seeking to deepen their bond with the Holy Light.",["al"]={"who is tiza","tiza battleforge lore","paladin trainer tiza"},["q"]="Who is Tiza Battleforge?"},{["a"]="She is located in the Hall of Mysteries, the center of spiritual and arcane learning situated in the Mystic Ward of Ironforge.",["al"]={"tiza location","where is tiza battleforge","hall of mysteries paladin trainer"},["q"]="Where can I find Tiza Battleforge?"},{["a"]="The Tome of Divinity is a sacred instructional text containing the core virtues and teachings of the Holy Light. Tiza gives it to paladins so they may study its lessons before embarking on practical trials of charity, courage, and mercy.",["al"]={"tome of divinity tiza","tiza book quest","what is tome of divinity"},["q"]="What is the Tome of Divinity she gives to paladins?"},{["a"]="Her husband, Muiredon Battleforge, faces hostile threats from the Dark Iron dwarves while trying to assist his companion Narm Faulk. Tiza uses this crisis to test an initiate's combat bravery and their readiness to use the Symbol of Life to bring fallen comrades back from the brink of death.",["al"]={"tiza husband quest","muiredon battleforge connection","why help muiredon"},["q"]="Why does Tiza send paladins to help her husband Muiredon?"},{["a"]="Upon completing her trials of charity and rescuing Muiredon's fallen comrade, Tiza grants the initiate the power of Redemption, the paladin's sacred rite of resurrection.",["al"]={"tiza paladin spell","what spell does tiza teach","resurrection paladin trainer ironforge"},["q"]="What ability does Tiza teach worthy paladins?"},{["a"]="Brandur Ironhammer is a fellow dwarven paladin trainer stationed alongside her in Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries. Tiza once candidly pointed out to Brandur that his jealousy was a spiritual weakness, prompting him to swear to her that he would strive to overcome it.",["al"]={"tiza and brandur","brandur ironhammer tiza","brandur jealousy"},["q"]="What is her connection to Brandur Ironhammer?"}},["kw"]={"dwarf","hall of mysteries","ironforge","muiredon battleforge","mystic ward","paladin","redemption","silver hand","tiza battleforge","tome of divinity"},["n"]="Tiza Battleforge",["s"]="Tiza Battleforge is a veteran dwarven paladin of the Knights of the Silver Hand stationed within Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries. Renowned for her steadfast devotion and insight, she guides young dwarven paladins along the path of virtue, charity, and self-sacrifice. Through study of the sacred texts and trials in the field, she tests whether initiates are truly ready to wield the Light's gift of resurrection.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Within the serene chambers of the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge, Tiza Battleforge stands as one of the most respected dwarven paladins of the Knights of the Silver Hand. Initiates across the Alliance—directed by tutors such as Brandur Ironhammer in Ironforge, Azar Stronghammer in Dun Morogh, and Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind—are sent to her to advance their spiritual education. Tiza believes that the Holy Light demands more than martial skill; it requires humble service, compassion, and unwavering fortitude against the encroaching darkness of the Scourge and other threats.",["t"]="Mentor of the Mystic Ward"},{["b"]="When young paladins arrive seeking deeper mysteries, Tiza presents them with the Tome of Divinity. Once the text has been studied, she dispatches them to perform tangible acts of selfless charity, starting by aiding those in humble need like John Turner. She then challenges initiates to put their faith and prowess on the line to aid her husband, Muiredon Battleforge, against the regional threat of the Dark Iron dwarves. Those who conquer these tests and revive fallen allies with the Symbol of Life are deemed worthy by Tiza to wield the sacred art of resurrection.",["t"]="The Trials of Divinity"}}}}}
t["npc:tonga-runetotem"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,374,25.507.0,32.602.1,21.498.0,23.213.0,43.177.0,55.167.1,37.199.0,45.178.0,82.214.0",["h"]="262a3b",["n"]="Tonga Runatótem",["s"]="Tonga Runatótem. Tonga Runatótem es un sabio druida tauren apostado junto a la posada de El Cruce, en Los Baldíos. Enviado desde Cima del Trueno, investiga una corrupción antinatural que se filtra en los escasos oasis de la región y enferma a la fauna autóctona. Sus pesquisas buscan rastrear el origen de esta perturbación espiritual antes de que el delicado ecosistema colapse por completo. Entre el polvo y el bullicioso comercio de El Cruce, Tonga Runatótem mantiene una discreta vigilia. Enviado desde las altas mesetas de Mulgore por los ancianos de su pueblo en Cima del Trueno, Tonga posee un profundo conocimiento de la árida sabana. Donde otros solo ven matorrales yermos y bestias depredadoras, él percibe las sutiles corrientes de la salud de la tierra. En tiempos recientes, esas corrientes se han deteriorado de forma alarmante, lo que le ha llevado a reclutar a viajeros capaces para investigar el núcleo vital de la sabana: sus oasis aislados.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,1,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="For tauren druids learning their craft, Tonga represents the practical application of Cenarion teachings, demonstrating how to diagnose and cleanse blighted ecosystems far from Moonglade.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde relies on Tonga's ecological investigations to ensure their primary thoroughfare through the Barrens remains habitable and protected from subterranean magical threats.",["race:Tauren"]="Tonga exemplifies the tauren commitment to the Earth Mother, working diligently to safeguard the fragile water sources that keep life alive across the parched plains."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Tonga is a tauren druid located near the inn at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He acts as an investigator sent by his elders in Thunder Bluff to study the strange natural corruptions spreading across the savannah.",["al"]={"tonga runetotem","who is tonga","crossroads druid"},["q"]="Who is Tonga Runetotem?"},{["a"]="He is investigating the unnatural emergence of strange vapors, mutated beasts, and tainted waters within the Barrens oases, including the Forgotten Pools and the Stagnant Oasis.",["al"]={"what is tonga doing","tonga quest goal","why investigate oases"},["q"]="What is Tonga investigating in the Barrens?"},{["a"]="Through studying altered creatures and water fissures, Tonga deduces that the magical taint infecting the oases originates deep underground within the Wailing Caverns.",["al"]={"source of oasis corruption","where is the taint from","wailing caverns connection"},["q"]="Where does Tonga believe the corruption is coming from?"},{["a"]="They share the Runetotem name, and Tonga sends word of the Barrens' troubles to Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem, the elder druid on Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise, but no source says whether they are related.",["al"]={"is he related to hamuul","runetotem family","hamuul relation"},["q"]="Is Tonga related to Hamuul Runetotem?"},{["a"]="Using teachings from Moonglade alongside local reagents, Tonga prepares curative salves to treat poisoned gazelles and counteract toxins flowing from sources like Dreadmist Peak.",["al"]={"gazelle cure","tonga curing sick","dreadmist peak poison"},["q"]="What does Tonga do for the poisoned wildlife?"},{["a"]="The Crossroads serves as the central hub of the northern Barrens, placing Tonga in close proximity to the affected oases while providing access to adventurers who can venture into dangerous territory on his behalf.",["al"]={"why crossroads","why is tonga here"},["q"]="Why is Tonga stationed at the Crossroads instead of Camp Taurajo or Thunder Bluff?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","crossroads","druid","forgotten pools","oases","runetotem","stagnant oasis","tonga","wailing caverns"},["n"]="Tonga Runetotem",["s"]="Tonga Runetotem is a knowledgeable tauren druid stationed outside the inn at the Crossroads in the Barrens. Dispatched from Thunder Bluff, he investigates an unnatural corruption seeping into the region's sparse oases and sickening the native wildlife. His research aims to trace the spiritual disturbance back to its origin before the delicate ecosystem collapses entirely.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Amid the dust and bustling commerce of the Crossroads, Tonga Runetotem keeps a quiet vigil. Sent down from the high mesas of Mulgore by his elders in Thunder Bluff, Tonga possesses an intimate understanding of the arid savannah. Where others see only barren scrub and predatory beasts, he reads the subtle currents of the land's health. In recent times, those currents have soured dramatically, compelling him to recruit capable travelers to investigate the heart of the savannah's life: its isolated oases.",["t"]="Watcher at the Crossroads"},{["b"]="The Barrens depends entirely on its scattered water sources, but the waters of the Forgotten Pools and the Stagnant Oasis have turned volatile. Strange bubbles of magical vapor rise to the surface, and the creatures drinking from them have begun mutating into aberrant, aggressive forms. Tonga works tirelessly to collect plant and creature samples, seeking to understand whether this malady is natural rot or the work of an intrusive power. His findings increasingly point toward deep subterranean fissures, connecting the poisoned pools directly to the subterranean labyrinths of the Wailing Caverns.",["t"]="Tainted Waters and Warped Beasts"},{["b"]="Bearing the proud name of the Runetotem clan, Tonga carries the heavy druidic heritage championed by Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem. While Archdruid Hamuul maintains relations with the Cenarion Circle and studies in the sacred groves of Moonglade, scouts like Tonga are the eyes and hands on the frontier. Tonga calls upon Moonglade's traditional botanical wisdom to compound healing salves and counter poisons, ensuring the young tauren druidic tradition proves its vital worth to the fledgling Horde.",["t"]="The Runetotem Lineage"}}}}}
t["npc:turak-runetotem"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,354,24.449.0,20.481.0,20.464.0,33.144.0,41.225.0,40.201.0,51.164.0,45.251.0,64.222.0",["h"]="24fa8b",["n"]="Turak Runatótem",["s"]="Turak Runatótem. Turak Runatótem es un venerado instructor de druidas tauren que reside en la Sala de los Ancestros, en lo alto del Alto de los Ancestros de Cima del Trueno. Como asistente de confianza del archidruida Hamuul Runatótem, guía a los tauren novicios por las sendas sagradas de la naturaleza y el equilibrio. A través de Turak, los jóvenes druidas emprenden pruebas fundamentales para comulgar con los espíritus y dominar los aspectos animales. Dentro de los serenos confines de la Sala de los Ancestros, Turak Runatótem destaca como uno de los mentores druídicos más destacados de la Horda. Renombrado por su profunda paciencia y su temperamento equilibrado, asiste al archidruida Hamuul Runatótem en revivir las antiguas artes druídicas entre el pueblo tauren. Turak se asegura de que cada aspirante a druida honre la voluntad de la Madre Tierra, enseñando que el poder físico siempre debe fundamentarse en el respeto espiritual y la armonía con la naturaleza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="For tauren druids, Turak Runetotem is the pillar of early training, granting the ability to teleport to Moonglade and testing aspirants until they earn their Bear and Aquatic forms.",["faction:Horde"]="Turak plays a vital part in anchoring nature magic within the Horde, training guardians capable of combating blights, environmental corruption, and the lingering scars across Kalimdor.",["race:Tauren"]="As a member of the Runetotem tribe, Turak embodies the revival of druidic customs among the tauren following the Third War, helping his people reclaim their ancient harmony with the Earthmother."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Turak Runetotem is located on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, stationed inside the tent of the Hall of Elders alongside Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem.",["al"]={"turak location","where is turak runetotem","turak runetotem thunder bluff"},["q"]="Where can I find Turak Runetotem?"},{["a"]="He serves as the primary quest giver and instructor for young tauren druids. He teaches them to commune with Moonglade, unlocks their Bear and Aquatic forms through sacred trials, and instructs them in curing natural poisons.",["al"]={"what does turak teach","turak druid trainer","turak role"},["q"]="What role does Turak play for new druids?"},{["a"]="Turak teaches novice druids the spell to teleport directly to the sacred grove of Moonglade, directing them to the Cenarion Circle's representative, Dendrite Starblaze, for advanced spiritual guidance.",["al"]={"turak moonglade","how does turak know dendrite","teleport moonglade turak"},["q"]="What is Turak's connection to Moonglade?"},{["a"]="Both belong to the venerable Runetotem tribe. Turak serves directly under Archdruid Hamuul as one of his most trusted assistants and teachers in the Hall of Elders.",["al"]={"is turak related to hamuul","hamuul and turak"},["q"]="How is Turak related to Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem?"},{["a"]="Turak sends students to Dendrite Starblaze in Moonglade to learn about poison, and Dendrite dispatches them to help with a rash of animal poisonings around the Crossroads. When they return, Turak rewards them with the power to cure poison permanently.",["al"]={"turak crossroads","turak poison quest","power over poison"},["q"]="Why does Turak send druids to the Crossroads?"},{["a"]="Turak openly shares that when he first walked the path to become a Druid of the Claw, his communion with the Great Bear Spirit was bewildering yet profoundly intense, an experience that deepened his reverence for the form.",["al"]={"turak bear spirit","turak path of the claw"},["q"]="What was Turak's personal experience with the Great Bear Spirit?"}},["kw"]={"aquatic form","bear form","dendrite starblaze","druid","elder rise","hall of elders","hamuul","lunaclaw","moonglade","runetotem","thunder bluff","turak"},["n"]="Turak Runetotem",["s"]="Turak Runetotem is a revered tauren druid trainer residing in the Hall of Elders atop Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise. Serving as a trusted assistant to Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem, he guides novice tauren along the sacred paths of nature and balance. Through Turak, young druids undertake foundational trials to commune with spirits and master animal aspects.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Within the serene confines of the Hall of Elders, Turak Runetotem stands as one of the Horde's foremost druidic mentors. Renowned for his deep patience and balanced demeanor, he assists Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem in reviving the ancient druidic arts among the tauren people. Turak ensures that every aspiring druid honors the will of the Earthmother, teaching that physical power must always be grounded in spiritual respect and harmony with nature.",["t"]="Voice of the Earthmother"},{["b"]="When a fledgling druid is prepared to embrace animal forms, Turak directs them into the wider world. He initiates their communion with the Cenarion Circle, teaching the art of teleporting across Kalimdor to the sacred haven of Moonglade. Recalling the bewilderment and intensity of his own youthful audience with the Great Bear Spirit, Turak tests his students' courage by sending them to face Lunaclaw and obtain the strength of body and heart needed to walk the Path of the Claw.",["t"]="The Path of the Claw"},{["b"]="Turak's guidance expands beyond primal combat forms to environmental stewardship. He sends his disciples back to Dendrite Starblaze to learn about poison, and Dendrite dispatches them to a rash of animal poisonings near the Crossroads, a situation that surprises even Turak. Through these trials, along with the arduous rituals beneath the tides to awaken the aquatic form, Turak shapes novices into enduring protectors capable of healing Azeroth's deepest wounds.",["t"]="Guardians of Balance"}}}}}
t["npc:twilight-lord-kelris"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,288,18.530.0,19.441.0,23.377.1,28.202.0,38.237.0,44.195.0,38.207.1,38.141.0,25.204.0",["h"]="c5eb06",["n"]="Señor Crepuscular Kelris",["s"]="Señor Crepuscular Kelris. El Señor Crepuscular Kelris es un brujo orco y un líder de alto rango dentro del culto del Martillo Crepuscular que opera en las profundidades de las Cavernas de Brazanegra. Desde su posición en Santuario Lunar, dirige oscuros rituales y cuida de la hidra primordial Aku'mai, con el objetivo de marcar el comienzo de un reinado de caos cósmico. El Señor Crepuscular Kelris dirige a los cultistas del Martillo Crepuscular que se apoderaron de las ruinas sumergidas de las Cavernas de Brazanegra. Durante años, Kelris escapó de la mirada vigilante de Darnassus, evadiendo al Alba Argenta y ganándose una sombría reputación: cada vez que una malicia ancestral se agitaba en Kalimdor, se sospechaba que Kelris la había orquestado. En lugar de servir a señores de la guerra o clanes, este orco se ha consagrado por entero a los Dioses Antiguos, buscando destruir la civilización mortal y devolver Azeroth a un estado de caos absoluto y primordial.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,1,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="While typical warlocks barter with demons of the Burning Legion, Kelris demonstrates the dark, trance-induced shadow magic born from yielding to Old God whispers.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Argent Dawn operating from Darnassus seeks the end of Kelris's elusive career of stirring dark cults and terror across northern Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="Elders and shamans view Kelris as a cautionary abomination—an orc who abandoned the elements and ancestral spirits to grovel before ancient cosmic horrors.",["race:NightElf"]="Kelris's blasphemous rituals actively despoil the sacred Moonshrine Sanctum, desecrating an ancient elven temple dedicated to Elune."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Twilight Lord Kelris is an orc sorcerer who commands the Twilight's Hammer presence in Blackfathom Deeps. He coordinates cult activity throughout the sunken temple and is deeply devoted to the Old Gods.",["al"]={"kelris lore","who is kelris","kelris background"},["q"]="Who is Twilight Lord Kelris?"},{["a"]="The Argent Dawn views Kelris as an elusive instigator of malice throughout Kalimdor. Though he was once believed dead or missing, his hand was discovered behind numerous dark plots across the continent, making his elimination a priority.",["al"]={"argent dawn kelris","why kill kelris","blackfathom villainy reason"},["q"]="Why is the Argent Dawn hunting Kelris?"},{["a"]="Kelris believes the three-headed hydra Aku'mai is a direct herald of the Old Gods and his path to eternal life. He personally nurtures the monster, offering it live sacrifices to fuel its growth.",["al"]={"kelris and akumai","why is kelris feeding akumai"},["q"]="What is Kelris doing with the hydra Aku'mai?"},{["a"]="Behind Kelris sits an altar with four ceremonial candles. Lighting these candles unbinds the sanctum's protective wards, summoning waves of Aku'mai's servants and opening the sealed gate to the beast's lair.",["al"]={"kelris candles","altar of kelris","moonshrine candles"},["q"]="What happens after Kelris is defeated?"},{["a"]="Kelris wields potent shadow spells, mental domination, and a magical slumber that can incapacitate his enemies while his dark rites continue.",["al"]={"kelris abilities","kelris spells"},["q"]="What powers does Kelris use in combat?"},{["a"]="Bashana Runetotem is an ally investigating the corruption in Blackfathom Deeps who warns adventurers of Kelris's obsession with Old God worship and his desire to plunge the world back into primeval chaos.",["al"]={"bashana runetotem kelris","tauren hunter kelris"},["q"]="Who is Bashana Runetotem?"}},["kw"]={"aku'mai","argent dawn","blackfathom deeps","kelris","moonshrine sanctum","old gods","twilight lord","twilight's hammer"},["n"]="Twilight Lord Kelris",["s"]="Twilight Lord Kelris is an orc warlock and high-ranking leader within the Twilight's Hammer cult operating deep inside Blackfathom Deeps. From his perch in the Moonshrine Sanctum, he leads dark rituals and tends to the primordial hydra Aku'mai, aiming to usher in a reign of cosmic chaos.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Twilight Lord Kelris directs the cultists of the Twilight's Hammer who seized the sunken ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. For years, Kelris slipped through the grasp of watchful eyes in Darnassus, evading the Argent Dawn and earning a grim reputation: whenever ancient malice stirred across Kalimdor, Kelris was suspected of orchestrating it. Rather than serving warlords or clans, this orc has pledged himself entirely to the Old Gods, seeking to unmake mortal civilization and return Azeroth to a state of absolute, primordial chaos.",["t"]="Herald of the Void"},{["b"]="Within the Moonshrine Sanctum, Kelris oversees the worship and cultivation of Aku'mai, a vicious three-headed hydra considered a herald and favored pet of the Old Gods. Convinced that raising this abomination will unlock his own immortality and signal the return of his masters, Kelris personally monitors its growth. To sate the creature's bottomless hunger, he feeds it captured sacrifices and even disobedient cultists from his own ranks.",["t"]="Keeper of the Beast"},{["b"]="Kelris commands potent shadow magic capable of seizing minds and plunging intruders into deep, unnatural sleep. He conducts constant prayers before a corrupted altar surrounded by candles that channel dark energies. Those attempting to strike down Kelris must not only defeat the cult leader, but also navigate the latent horrors that stir once his ritualistic vigil is broken.",["t"]="Dark Trance and Slumber"}}}}}
t["npc:tyrande-whisperwind"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,417,26.614.0,32.561.0,29.602.0,27.298.0,36.234.0,55.303.0,32.281.0,45.279.0,33.304.0",["h"]="4c544c",["n"]="Tyrande Susurravientos",["s"]="Tyrande Susurravientos. Tyrande Susurravientos es la suma sacerdotisa de Elune y la líder suprema de los elfos de la noche. Junto a su amado, el archidruida Malfurión Tempestira, guio a su pueblo a través de la cataclísmica Guerra de los Ancestros y durante los diez milenios de la Larga Vigilia. Gobernando ahora desde las ramas sagradas de Teldrassil, comanda a las Hermanas de Elune y dirige al ejército de centinelas en defensa de la naturaleza sagrada de Kalimdor. Nacida en la antigua ciudad de Suramar, Tyrande creció junto a los hermanos gemelos Malfurión e Illidan Tempestira. Mientras los hermanos se inclinaron por el druidismo y la hechicería, Tyrande entró al servicio de Elune como novicia en la hermandad. Cuando la demoníaca Legión Ardiente invadió Azeroth por primera vez durante la Guerra de los Ancestros, la moribunda suma sacerdotisa Dejahna eligió a Tyrande como su sucesora. Bendecida con el favor directo de la Diosa de la Luna, Tyrande transformó a las Hermanas en una radiante fuerza de combate, empuñando tanto la restauración divina como la abrasadora cólera lunar para rescatar a su pueblo del borde de la aniquilación total.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="While Malfurion slumbers in the Emerald Dream, Tyrande coordinates closely with the Cenarion Circle to protect sacred groves and nurture Teldrassil.",["class:Priest"]="As the living vessel of Elune's divine favor, Tyrande embodies the pinnacle of kaldorei priesthood, calling down lunar stars and mending wounds through pure faith.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though historically reclusive and fiercely independent, Tyrande leads the night elves within the Alliance to secure mutual defense against Kalimdor's growing perils.",["faction:Horde"]="To the Horde, Tyrande is a formidable, uncompromising adversary who has commanded the Sentinels to violently resist resource harvesting across Ashenvale.",["race:NightElf"]="Tyrande is your supreme leader and High Priestess. For over ten thousand years, she has kept vigil over your race, championing the light of Elune through every trial."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Tyrande Whisperwind is the High Priestess of Elune and the supreme spiritual and political leader of the night elves. She has guided her people for over ten thousand years from the War of the Ancients through the Third War, and currently leads the kaldorei from the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",["al"]={"who is tyrande","tyrande whisperwind lore","night elf leader"},["q"]="Who is Tyrande Whisperwind?"},{["a"]="Tyrande resides in the capital city of Darnassus, situated high in the branches of the world tree Teldrassil. She presides from the upper sanctuary of the Temple of the Moon, surrounded by the Priestesses of Elune and Sentinel guards.",["al"]={"where is tyrande","tyrande location","where to find tyrande"},["q"]="Where does Tyrande reside right now?"},{["a"]="Tyrande and Malfurion Stormrage are lifelong partners who have guided the night elf civilization together for ten millennia. Though both Malfurion and his twin brother Illidan sought her love in their youth, Tyrande chose Malfurion, whose deep devotion to balance and nature mirrored her faith in Elune.",["al"]={"tyrande malfurion","is tyrande married","tyrande and illidan"},["q"]="What is the relationship between Tyrande and Malfurion?"},{["a"]="The Sisterhood of Elune is the ancient religious order of night elf priestesses dedicated to worshiping the Moon Goddess. Under Tyrande's leadership as High Priestess, the sisters serve not only as healers and spiritual guides, but also as fierce martial commanders and combatants.",["al"]={"sisterhood of elune","priestesses of elune","tyrande priests"},["q"]="What is the Sisterhood of Elune?"},{["a"]="During the ten thousand years after the Sundering, while Malfurion and the male druids slumbered in the Emerald Dream, Tyrande established and commanded the Sentinels. She patrolled the wilds of Kalimdor, hunted remaining satyrs and demons, and kept her people safe in isolation.",["al"]={"what was the long vigil","tyrande long vigil","sentinel leader"},["q"]="What role did Tyrande play in the Long Vigil?"},{["a"]="During the Third War, the orcs entered Ashenvale and began clear-cutting sacred forests, slaying the demigod Cenarius under the influence of demon blood. While an uneasy truce was struck at Mount Hyjal, the Horde's ongoing logging operations in Ashenvale ensure Tyrande keeps her Sentinels on high alert.",["al"]={"tyrande horde","why does tyrande hate orcs","night elves vs horde"},["q"]="Why is Tyrande wary of the Horde?"}},["kw"]={"darnassus","elune","kaldorei","malfurion","priestess","sentinels","teldrassil","tyrande","whisperwind"},["n"]="Tyrande Whisperwind",["s"]="Tyrande Whisperwind is the High Priestess of Elune and the supreme leader of the night elves. Alongside her beloved, the Archdruid Malfurion Stormrage, she guided her people through the cataclysmic War of the Ancients and ten millennia of the Long Vigil. Now governing from the sacred boughs of Teldrassil, she commands the Sisterhood of Elune and directs the Sentinel army in defense of Kalimdor's sacred wilderness.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Born in the ancient city of Suramar, Tyrande grew up alongside the twin brothers Malfurion and Illidan Stormrage. While the brothers followed druidism and sorcery, Tyrande entered the service of Elune as a novice in the sisterhood. When the demonic Burning Legion first invaded Azeroth during the War of the Ancients, the dying High Priestess Dejahna chose Tyrande as her successor. Blessed with direct favor from the Moon Goddess, Tyrande transformed the Sisterhood into a radiant fighting force, wielding both divine restoration and searing lunar wrath to deliver her people from the brink of total annihilation.",["t"]="Chosen of the Moon Goddess"},{["b"]="Following the Great Sundering and the sealing of the Well of Eternity, Malfurion and the druids entered the Emerald Dream for deep, prolonged hibernations. Tyrande took upon herself the lonely burden of defending their recovering realm. She organized the Sentinels—an elite cadre of warrior-women who patrolled Kalimdor's forests for ten thousand years. Throughout this Long Vigil, she stood watchful guard over ancient evils and lingering demonic remnants, maintaining unbroken faith in Elune while she waited centuries between brief reunions with Malfurion.",["t"]="The Long Vigil and the Sentinels"},{["b"]="When the Burning Legion returned during the Third War, Tyrande acted decisively to wake the sleeping druids and face the catastrophic threat. Overcoming fierce mistrust toward the newly arrived orcs and humans, she helped forge the desperate coalition at Mount Hyjal, sacrificing the night elves' immortality atop Nordrassil to shatter Archimonde. With Mount Hyjal scarred and Malfurion once again occupied with safeguarding the Emerald Dream, Tyrande governs the kaldorei from the grand Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, watching cautiously over both Horde incursions and the growing Alliance alliance.",["t"]="The Third War and a New Haven"}}}}}
t["npc:verdan-the-everliving"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="21,366,27.311.0,24.418.1,32.171.0,37.216.0,54.216.0,47.137.0,32.198.0,39.115.0",["h"]="cbf0da",["n"]="Verdan el Eterno",["s"]="Verdan el Eterno. Verdan el Eterno es una colosal bestia del pantano que acecha en las profundidades de los túneles verdes de las Cuevas de los Lamentos. Antaño un pacífico protector de los manantiales subterráneos y de la flora, fue corrompido por la pesadilla despierta que irradiaba del druida durmiente Naralex. Ahora vinculado a los corrompidos Druidas del Colmillo, Verdan ataca con violencia a todo aquel que se adentre en sus húmedas hondonadas. Mucho antes de que Naralex llegara para aprovechar los manantiales naturales de Los Baldíos, Verdan se formó a partir de la frondosa vegetación, el limo y la humedad que llenaban las cuevas. Considerado el espíritu guardián original del oasis subterráneo, Verdan era un elemental antiguo y apacible que velaba por la flora subterránea.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Verdan's fall is a tragic reminder of what happens when natural elemental wardens are poisoned by a corrupted Emerald Dream.",["class:Shaman"]="As an elemental spirit of earth and water grown warped and violent, putting down Verdan is an act of restoring balance to the fractured elements of the Barrens.",["faction:Horde"]="Because the Wailing Caverns sit at the heart of the Barrens, defeating dangerous beasts like Verdan is essential to protecting nearby crossroads and settlements."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Verdan is a massive bog beast, an elemental being animated out of plant matter, peat, and subterranean mire. He formed naturally from the rich flora of the caves long ago.",["al"]={"verdan monster type","what is verdan","verdan race"},["q"]="What kind of creature is Verdan?"},{["a"]="Verdan was once a peaceful guardian of the caverns, but the nightmare emanating from the slumbering Archdruid Naralex corrupted his mind. Now maddened, he perceives all outside intruders as trespassers to be crushed.",["al"]={"why does verdan attack","verdan hostile","is verdan evil"},["q"]="Why is Verdan hostile to adventurers?"},{["a"]="Both Verdan and the Druids of the Fang fell victim to the same corrupting nightmare. Sharing this twisted vision, Verdan acts as an ally and enforcer for the insane druids, guarding the deeper reaches of the caverns.",["al"]={"verdan druids of the fang","verdan fang connection"},["q"]="What is Verdan's connection to the Druids of the Fang?"},{["a"]="Verdan dwells in a cavernous, mossy chamber deep in the winding paths of the Wailing Caverns, past several of the corrupted Fang leaders.",["al"]={"where is verdan","verdan location","how to find verdan"},["q"]="Where in the Wailing Caverns is Verdan located?"},{["a"]="There is no known way to cleanse Verdan. The nightmare took deep root in his elemental form, leaving adventurers no choice but to destroy the hulking beast to ensure safe passage through the cavern.",["al"]={"can verdan be saved","save verdan","purify verdan"},["q"]="Can Verdan be cured or cleansed?"},{["a"]="The origin of his epithet is unknown. Verdan is an ancient bog beast formed from the Wailing Caverns' lush foliage.",["al"]={"why everliving","everliving meaning","verdan name origin"},["q"]="Why was Verdan called 'the Everliving'?"}},["kw"]={"bog beast","druids of the fang","elemental","everliving","naralex","nightmare","verdan","wailing caverns"},["n"]="Verdan the Everliving",["s"]="Verdan the Everliving is a colossal bog beast lurking deep within the verdant tunnels of the Wailing Caverns. Once a peaceful protector of the underground springs and flora, he was twisted by the waking nightmare radiating from the sleeping druid Naralex. Now bound to the corrupted Druids of the Fang, Verdan violently attacks any who venture into his damp hollows.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Long before Naralex arrived to tap into the natural springs of the Barrens, Verdan was formed from the overgrown foliage, silt, and moisture filling the caves. Thought to be the original guardian spirit of the subterranean oasis, Verdan was an ancient, gentle elemental keeping watch over the underground flora.",["t"]="Guardian of the Lush Depths"},{["b"]="When Naralex attempted to cultivate the dry Barrens into a lush paradise, his ritual fractured into a vivid nightmare within the Emerald Dream. The resulting corruption bled through the subterranean waters, tainting everything living inside the cavern. Verdan could not resist the pervasive blight; his gentle temperament vanished, leaving behind an enormous, hostile brute sworn to protect the mad Druids of the Fang.",["t"]="Twisted by the Nightmare"}}}}}
t["npc:verner-osgood"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,267,22.470.0,18.385.0,21.199.0,41.198.0,46.199.0,48.185.0,50.193.0,37.195.0",["h"]="7e0331",["n"]="Verner Bonmete",["s"]="Verner Bonmete. Verner Bonmete es el herrero residente de Villa del Lago, apostado justo a las afueras de la herrería del pueblo. Compaginando el comercio civil local con las abrumadoras exigencias del ejército de Ventormenta, trabaja sin descanso para mantener a los caballos herrados y a los defensores armados en medio de incesantes incursiones de gnolls. Junto a la forja en el centro de Villa del Lago, Verner Bonmete representa la tensa columna vertebral industrial de las Montañas Crestagrana. Con la tarea de forjar suministros básicos como herraduras para las monturas locales, Verner ve cómo sus existencias son confiscadas constantemente para fabricar armas y armaduras para la Guardia de Ventormenta. Con el reino extendiendo sus fronteras hasta el límite y las guarniciones locales carentes de suministros, herreros independientes como Verner deben cargar con el peso logístico de la defensa del reino.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Towns like Lakeshire depend on local craftsmen like Verner to survive as Stormwind's military aid remains dangerously constrained.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Verner embodies the gritty reality of rural smithing, balancing civilian shoeing with the harsh quotas demanded by garrison defense.",["race:Human"]="Osgood represents the enduring resilience of the Kingdom of Stormwind's common folk, holding ground against gnolls and shortages alike."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Verner Osgood is the local blacksmith operating the forge in Lakeshire. He handles metalwork and horse shoeing for the town while attempting to meet the heavy equipment demands of the local garrison.",["al"]={"verner osgood","lakeshire blacksmith","who is verner"},["q"]="Who is Verner Osgood?"},{["a"]="The town's supply of iron is continually requisitioned to forge weapons and armor for the Stormwind Guard stationed in Redridge, leaving Verner with barely enough metal to care for the local horses.",["al"]={"verner out of iron","price of shoes quest lore","why no horseshoes"},["q"]="Why is Verner low on horseshoes and iron?"},{["a"]="Gnoll raiding parties roam closely around Lakeshire, snatching away Verner's horses whenever they wander away from town. He seeks retribution and safety by hiring adventurers to eliminate the beasts.",["al"]={"verner gnoll problem","why does verner hate gnolls"},["q"]="What problem does Verner have with the gnolls?"},{["a"]="Yowler is the menacing leader of the local gnoll packs in the hills. Verner wants him slain to break the coordination of the raiders who terrorize the township and slaughter his horses.",["al"]={"who is yowler","verner yowler quest"},["q"]="Who is Yowler and why does Verner want him dead?"},{["a"]="Verner operates under the civic authority of Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire, balancing civilian craft with the civic and martial needs commanded by the magistrate's beleaguered administration.",["al"]={"verner magistrate solomon","verner and the town leadership"},["q"]="What is Verner's connection to Magistrate Solomon?"},{["a"]="He shares a surname with several other tradesmen in the Kingdom of Stormwind, such as Donal and Basil Osgood, suggesting an established lineage of working-class human craftsmen across the region.",["al"]={"verner relatives","osgood family"},["q"]="Does Verner have family in Stormwind?"}},["kw"]={"blacksmith","gnolls","horses","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","redridge","verner osgood","yowler"},["n"]="Verner Osgood",["s"]="Verner Osgood is the resident blacksmith of Lakeshire, stationed just outside the town smithy. Balancing local civilian trade with the crushing demands of the Stormwind military, he works tirelessly to keep horses shod and defenders armed amid relentless gnoll raids.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing by the forge in central Lakeshire, Verner Osgood represents the strained industrial backbone of the Redridge Mountains. Tasked with crafting basic supplies like horseshoes for local mounts, Verner finds his stock constantly co-opted to manufacture weapons and armor for the Stormwind Guard. With the kingdom stretching its borders thin and local garrisons lacking supplies, independent smiths like Verner must carry the logistical burden of the realm's defense.",["t"]="The Anvil of Lakeshire"},{["b"]="Verner's troubles extend far beyond a shortage of iron. The gnolls infesting the Redridge hills routinely ambush livestock, carrying off working horses whenever they stray outside the town perimeter. Driven to exasperation by the destruction of his livelihood, Verner actively recruits traveling adventurers to cull the marauding packs and hunt down their ferocious packleader, Yowler.",["t"]="A Plague of Gnolls"}}}}}
t["npc:viktori-prism-antras"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,359,21.420.0,38.354.0,28.239.0,38.127.0,32.195.0,43.227.0,47.167.0,35.207.0",["h"]="90aa63",["n"]="Viktori Prism'Antras",["s"]="Viktori Prism'Antras. Viktori Prism'Antras es un excéntrico astrónomo aficionado que reside en una pequeña cabaña en la ladera con vistas a Villa Oscura. Mientras el pueblo que lo rodea sucumbe al pavor y a horrores inminentes, Viktori se concentra intensamente en construir un telescopio para contemplar los cielos con claridad. Para hacer realidad su visión, confía en viajeros intrépidos que le consigan piezas complejas basadas en esquemas gnómicos. Encaramado en la pendiente más allá del Nidal de Grifos, Viktori Prism'Antras pasa los días oteando desde la penumbra de Bosque del Ocaso. En medio de incursiones de no-muertos, arañas voraces y sombras acechantes, su obsesión se sitúa mucho más allá del asfixiante dosel. Sueña con construir un magnífico telescopio óptico capaz de enfocar las estrellas con brillantez, ofreciendo un sereno escape del espanto que envuelve a la aldea.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Assisting Viktori provides a rare, peaceful pursuit in Darkshire, helping an Alliance townsman seek wonder amidst pervasive tragedy.",["profession:Engineering"]="Tinkers will appreciate Viktori's endeavor, as building his precision viewing instrument relies entirely on sophisticated gnomish schematics.",["race:Gnome"]="Viktori's entire project rests on the ingenuity of the gnome inventor Cog Glitzspinner, showcasing the reach of gnomish engineering even in the most desolate human towns."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Viktori is an eccentric human stargazer residing in Darkshire. Rather than concerning himself with the town's immediate political or supernatural threats, he is singularly obsessed with constructing a powerful telescope to study the stars.",["al"]={"who is viktori","viktori prism'antras lore","viktori duskwood"},["q"]="Who is Viktori Prism'Antras?"},{["a"]="He lives in a small wooden hut up the hill just past the Darkshire gryphon master, located to the right as you ascend the path.",["al"]={"viktori prism'antras location","where is viktori","find viktori darkshire"},["q"]="Where can I find Viktori in Darkshire?"},{["a"]="Viktori is attempting to build an astronomical telescope using blueprints drawn up by his gnomish colleague Cog Glitzspinner, which requires several specialized lenses and components to assemble.",["al"]={"viktori telescope","look to the stars device","what does viktori make"},["q"]="What is Viktori trying to build?"},{["a"]="Despite the darkness and constant terror permeating Duskwood, Viktori is consumed by celestial curiosity. Focusing on the untainted majesty of the night sky provides him an intellectual refuge from the decaying land around him.",["al"]={"why darkshire telescope","why study stars in duskwood"},["q"]="Why is he studying the stars from Duskwood?"},{["a"]="The blueprints were engineered by Cog Glitzspinner, an inventive gnome acquaintance of Viktori who provided the schematics necessary to assemble the viewing apparatus.",["al"]={"cog glitzspinner","who made the telescope schematics"},["q"]="Who designed the plans for Viktori's telescope?"},{["a"]="No. Viktori is a civilian scholar rather than a warrior. He leaves the defense of the town to Commander Althea Ebonlocke and the Night Watch, preferring to dedicate all his energies to his astronomical work.",["al"]={"is viktori a night watchman","does viktori fight"},["q"]="Does Viktori help defend Darkshire?"}},["kw"]={"astronomy","cog glitzspinner","darkshire","duskwood","look to the stars","prism'antras","stargazer","telescope","viktori"},["n"]="Viktori Prism'Antras",["s"]="Viktori Prism'Antras is an eccentric stargazer residing in a small hillside hut overlooking Darkshire. While the town around him succumbs to dread and looming horrors, Viktori focuses intently on building a telescope to view the heavens clearly. To realize his vision, he relies on adventurous travelers to acquire intricate parts based on gnomish schematics.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched up the slope just beyond the gryphon roost, Viktori Prism'Antras spends his days peering outward from the gloom of Duskwood. Amid undead incursions, ravenous spiders, and creeping shadows, his obsession lies far beyond the suffocating canopy. He dreams of building a magnificent optical telescope capable of bringing the stars into brilliant focus, offering a quiet escape from the dread that engulfs the hamlet.",["t"]="Eyes Upon the Heavens"},{["b"]="Constructing such a delicate apparatus is no simple matter in a cursed forest. Viktori works from blueprints provided by his gnomish friend, Cog Glitzspinner. To complete the device, he enlists passersby to track down rare lens-crafting materials and mechanical housings, ranging from finely cut glass to metal lenses scattered across perilous territory.",["t"]="Gnomish Schematics and Scattered Parts"}}}}}
t["npc:viscous-fallout"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,254,17.502.0,19.377.0,24.227.0,28.293.0,35.202.0,18.186.0,41.240.0,39.160.0",["h"]="35b809",["n"]="Radiactivo viscoso",["s"]="Radiactivo viscoso. El Radiactivo viscoso es un elemental de agua corrupto que vaga por los pasillos irradiados de Gnomeregan. Antaño un espíritu puro que habitaba los prístinos acuíferos de la ciudad, fue transformado en una monstruosidad tóxica por la devastadora liberación de radiación del Mekigeniero Termochufe. Antes de la caída de Gnomeregan, la capital gnoma dependía de complejas y sofisticadas vías fluviales y acuíferos subterráneos limpios para alimentar y mantener sus maravillas mecánicas. Un solitario elemental de agua moraba pacíficamente en este prístino suministro de agua. Cuando se abrieron los conductos de ventilación de radiación por el traicionero consejo del Mekigeniero Termochufe para aniquilar a los troggs invasores, la consiguiente contaminación química se filtró profundamente en los embalses de la ciudad, atrapando al elemental y corrompiendo su propia sustancia.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids view the creature as a living wound upon nature, illustrating the horrific consequences of reckless industrial contamination seeping into natural underground waters.",["class:Shaman"]="A shaman will recognize the perversion of the elemental plane, seeing in Viscous Fallout a pure water spirit driven mad and defiled by artificial toxic waste.",["race:Gnome"]="For gnomes, Viscous Fallout is a tragic reminder of the damage Mekgineer Thermaplugg inflicted upon their home, corrupting even the pristine subterranean springs that once sustained Gnomeregan."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Viscous Fallout is a water elemental mini-boss located inside the ruined city of Gnomeregan. Formerly a pure water spirit native to the city's deep aquifers, it became thoroughly tainted by toxic sludge and radioactive fallout.",["al"]={"who is viscous fallout","viscous fallout lore","what kind of mob is viscous fallout"},["q"]="What is Viscous Fallout?"},{["a"]="When Gnomeregan was flooded with radiation on Mekgineer Thermaplugg's treacherous advice to repel the trogg invasion, the contaminated runoff infiltrated the city's plumbing and aquifers. The trapped water elemental absorbed the deadly chemical stew, warping into an acidic, irradiated horror.",["al"]={"why is it green","why is the elemental toxic","how was viscous fallout created"},["q"]="How did it become corrupted?"},{["a"]="Viscous Fallout patrols the lower irradiated passages and runoff canals below the main entry paths of Gnomeregan, often blending in among the ordinary mutated slimes and toxic wastes infesting the area.",["al"]={"viscous fallout location","where to find viscous fallout","how to find viscous fallout"},["q"]="Where in Gnomeregan does it wander?"},{["a"]="The elemental is driven mad by relentless agony and toxic corruption. Stripped of its natural purity, it lashes out furiously at any living creature trespassing in the tainted waterways.",["al"]={"why does it attack","can it be saved"},["q"]="Why is it hostile?"},{["a"]="Gnomish refugees in Tinker Town inside Ironforge remember the complex waterways that once supported Gnomeregan. Items associated with the waterworks, such as the Hydrocane, are tied to these corrupted chambers and sought after for recovery.",["al"]={"hydrocane ironforge","gnome connection"},["q"]="Does it have any connection to Ironforge?"},{["a"]="No cure exists for the elemental. The radiation and toxic chemicals have permeated its form so entirely that destroying it is the only way to end its suffering.",["al"]={"can you cure viscous fallout","cleanse viscous fallout"},["q"]="Can the elemental be cleansed or cured?"}},["kw"]={"aquifer","gnomeregan","hydrocane","radiation","thermaplugg","tinker town","viscous fallout","water elemental"},["n"]="Viscous Fallout",["s"]="Viscous Fallout is a corrupted water elemental wandering the irradiated corridors of Gnomeregan. Once a pure spirit inhabiting the city's pristine aquifers, it was twisted into a toxic monstrosity by Mekgineer Thermaplugg's devastating radiation release.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the fall of Gnomeregan, the gnomish capital relied on sophisticated, intricate waterways and clean subterranean aquifers to power and sustain its mechanical marvels. A solitary water elemental dwelt peacefully within this pristine water supply. When the radiation vents were opened on Mekgineer Thermaplugg's treacherous advice to wipe out the invading troggs, the resulting chemical contamination seeped deep into the city's reservoirs, trapping the elemental and corrupting its very substance.",["t"]="A Polluted Spirit"},{["b"]="Now, the creature is little more than a living pool of toxic sludge, drifting aimlessly through the irradiated lower passages. Transformed into an embodiment of Thermaplugg's treachery, Viscous Fallout lashes out at anything in its path, consumed by constant pain and fury. Striking it down is a grim necessity for those venturing into Gnomeregan to cleanse the tainted depths.",["t"]="Agony in the Runoff"}}}}}
t["npc:warden-thelwater"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,296,22.486.0,20.477.1,24.164.0,30.250.0,31.166.0,56.235.0,37.149.0,36.147.0",["h"]="1a43a7",["n"]="Alcaide Thelagua",["s"]="Alcaide Thelagua. El Alcaide Thelagua es el asediado supervisor de Las Mazmorras, la prisión subterránea de máxima seguridad de Ciudad de Ventormenta. Sorprendido sin preparación cuando estalló un violento motín entre los prisioneros Defias, ahora recluta desesperadamente a aventureros capaces para sofocar la rebelión antes de que la noticia se extienda a la ciudad de arriba. Ocultas bajo los canales de Ventormenta, Las Mazmorras albergan a los malhechores más peligrosos del reino, ladronzuelos y conspiradores políticos. El Alcaide Thelagua tenía el encargo de mantenerlos encerrados a buen recaudo, pero una revuelta organizada pilló a los guardias completamente desprevenidos. Con los prisioneros superando a la seguridad y tomando el control de las celdas, Thelagua se vio atrincherado en la entrada, luchando por contener una insurrección armada justo debajo de las calles de la capital.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="For holy warriors dedicated to order and justice, Thelwater's desperate struggle to restore containment provides a direct call to bring righteous discipline to violent criminals.",["class:Rogue"]="Rogues entering the Stockade for Thelwater find themselves navigating the messy fallout of Defias intrigue and underground prison politics.",["faction:Alliance"]="Warden Thelwater represents the fragile order within Stormwind, relying on loyal Alliance champions to squash the prison mutiny before it threatens the capital's citizens."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Warden Thelwater is the human official stationed at the entrance of the Stockade in Stormwind City. He is responsible for managing the high-security prison complex.",["al"]={"thelwater","stockade warden","who is thelwater"},["q"]="Who is Warden Thelwater?"},{["a"]="A coordinated revolt broke out among the prisoners, primarily driven by incarcerated members of the Defias Brotherhood. The inmates overpowered the guards and took over the cellblocks, leaving Thelwater and his remaining men pinned near the entrance.",["al"]={"stockade riot","what happened in stockades","why is stockades broken"},["q"]="What happened to the Stockade?"},{["a"]="Bazil Thredd is the mastermind orchestrating the revolt from deep inside the prison. He commands the Defias inmates and directed the sudden strike against the guards.",["al"]={"stockade leader","who leads the uprising","who is bazil thredd"},["q"]="Who is leading the prison riot?"},{["a"]="Thelwater aims to resolve the disaster quietly. Broadcasting that Stormwind's most fortified dungeon fell to its own inmates would ignite widespread panic across the city, so he enlists discreet adventurers to clean up the mess inside.",["al"]={"why no guards","why hire adventurers","secret riot"},["q"]="Why hasn't the Stormwind City Guard intervened in force?"},{["a"]="The facility holds petty crooks, thieves, murderers, and dangerous political insurgents, most notably high-ranking members of the Defias Brotherhood.",["al"]={"stockade prisoners","who is in stockade","types of criminals"},["q"]="What kind of prisoners are kept here?"},{["a"]="He is stationed just outside the entrance of the Stockade, located near the canals between the Mage Quarter and Cathedral Square in Stormwind City.",["al"]={"thelwater location","where is warden","find thelwater"},["q"]="Where can Warden Thelwater be found?"}},["kw"]={"bazil thredd","defias","prison","riot","stockade","stormwind","thelwater","warden thelwater"},["n"]="Warden Thelwater",["s"]="Warden Thelwater is the besieged overseer of the Stockade, Stormwind City's underground maximum-security prison. Caught unprepared when a violent riot erupted among the Defias prisoners, he now desperately recruits capable adventurers to quell the rebellion before word spreads to the city above.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Hidden beneath the canals of Stormwind, the Stockade holds the kingdom's most dangerous miscreants, petty thieves, and political conspirators. Warden Thelwater was charged with keeping them securely locked away, but an organized revolt took the guards completely off guard. With the prisoners overwhelming security and taking control of the cells, Thelwater found himself barricaded at the threshold, struggling to contain an armed insurrection right beneath the streets of the capital.",["t"]="A Crisis in the Canals"},{["b"]="Rather than allowing panic to spill into the streets of Stormwind, Thelwater has chosen to handle the uprising with absolute discretion. The mastermind behind the breakout, Bazil Thredd, holds tremendous influence among the Defias Brotherhood locked inside. To prevent the riot from exposing wider vulnerabilities within Stormwind's governance, Thelwater relies on outside mercenaries to infiltrate the cellblocks, strike down the ringleaders, and quietly reclaim the facility.",["t"]="Containing the Truth"}}}}}
t["npc:william-pestle"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,300,17.463.0,16.405.0,27.380.1,22.199.0,34.82.0,41.174.0,35.175.1,54.180.0,58.173.1",["h"]="c519f3",["n"]="William Mortero",["s"]="William Mortero. William Mortero es un alquimista humano que se aloja en la Posada Orgullo de León, en Villadorada. Junto con su hermano Morgan, ayuda a regentar la botica en el Distrito de Mercaderes de Ventormenta. Con frecuencia contrata a aventureros de paso para reunir reactivos peculiares como velas de kobolds, kelp de múrlocs y suministros de hierbas. Mientras su hermano Morgan Mortero atiende el mostrador de la botica de los Mortero en el Distrito de Mercaderes de la Ciudad de Ventormenta, William opera desde la Posada Orgullo de León, en Villadorada. Estar destinado en el Bosque de Elwynn le permite trabajar estrechamente con los recolectores locales y conseguir las materias primas que las tiendas de la ciudad necesitan constantemente. Mantiene envíos regulares a la capital, asegurando que los ciudadanos de Ventormenta tengan un acceso constante a ungüentos reparadores, brebajes y polvos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,1,0,1},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="William helps keep the Trade District in Stormwind supplied with vital medicines and sundries, relying on Alliance recruits passing through Goldshire to secure materials from the surrounding forest.",["profession:Herbalism"]="For herbalists wandering through Goldshire, William Pestle represents the practical trade side of plant gathering, constantly turning wild growth and strange aquatic kelp into useful mixtures."},["faq"]={{["a"]="William Pestle is an alchemist and apothecary living at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. Alongside his brother Morgan in Stormwind City, he gathers and prepares alchemical supplies for the kingdom.",["al"]={"william pestle","goldshire alchemist","who is pestle"},["q"]="Who is William Pestle?"},{["a"]="He is located inside the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, situated in Elwynn Forest.",["al"]={"pestle location","where is william pestle","william pestle goldshire"},["q"]="Where can William Pestle be found?"},{["a"]="William collects the wax candles carried by kobolds in Elwynn's mines, melting them down and refining the tallow for his alchemical mixtures and general apothecary inventory.",["al"]={"why does pestle want candles","kobold candles use"},["q"]="What does William do with kobold candles?"},{["a"]="William uses Crystal Kelp harvested from local Elwynn lakes to formulate an Invisibility Liquor, which helps Maybell Maclure sneak past her family to see Tommy Joe Stonefield.",["al"]={"collecting kelp why","murloc kelp use"},["q"]="Why does William need Crystal Kelp?"},{["a"]="William and his brother Morgan run the apothecary in the Trade District of Stormwind City. William gathers ingredients in Goldshire and coordinates shipments back to the city shop.",["al"]={"pestle stormwind","william pestle apothecary shop"},["q"]="What is William Pestle's connection to Stormwind City?"},{["a"]="William is an old friend of Mildred Stonefield. He aids Tommy Joe Stonefield and Maybell Maclure by concocting a covert brew to help them bypass their families' bitter feud.",["al"]={"stonefield maclure pestle","william pestle love quest"},["q"]="How is William involved with the Stonefields and Maclures?"}},["kw"]={"apothecary","collecting kelp","goldshire","kobold candles","lion's pride inn","maclure","morgan pestle","pestle","stonefield","william pestle"},["n"]="William Pestle",["s"]="William Pestle is a human alchemist staying inside Goldshire's Lion's Pride Inn. Together with his brother Morgan, he helps run the apothecary shop in Stormwind's Trade District. He frequently employs traveling adventurers to gather odd reagents like kobold candles, murloc kelp, and herbal supplies.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While his brother Morgan Pestle manages the counter at Pestle's Apothecary in the Trade District of Stormwind City, William operates out of the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. Being stationed in Elwynn Forest allows him to work closely with local gatherers and secure raw materials that city shops constantly require. He maintains regular shipments back to the capital, ensuring Stormwind's citizens have steady access to restorative salves, draughts, and powders.",["t"]="Apothecary Abroad"},{["b"]="William's craft often demands unusual components that go beyond simple garden herbs. He frequently commissions newcomers to gather wax candles carried by Elwynn's infesting kobolds, as well as crystal kelp taken from the murlocs of Crystal Lake, just east of Goldshire. Although such concoctions seem bizarre to the uninitiated, William insists these strange ingredients possess potent alchemical virtues.",["t"]="Curious Reagents"},{["b"]="Beyond his standard trade, William is an old friend of Mildred Stonefield. When the young lovers Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield find themselves caught between their bitterly feuding farmstead families, William agrees to brew an Invisibility Liquor. Using the kelp gathered from local waters, his draft allows Maybell to slip away unnoticed and rendezvous with Tommy Joe.",["t"]="A Concoction for Young Love"}}}}}
t["npc:wizbang-cranktoggle"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,332,24.396.0,19.483.0,37.112.0,47.166.0,19.209.0,39.104.0,59.191.0,44.173.0",["h"]="9a94ae",["n"]="Maniveo Zumbang",["s"]="Maniveo Zumbang. Maniveo Zumbang es un excéntrico ingeniero gnomo que reside en la planta superior de la posada de Auberdine. A pesar de encontrarse lejos de las salas repletas de engranajes de Gnomeregan o Forjaz, ha enfocado su ingenio mecánico en instalar y mantener dispositivos de comunicación automatizados conocidos como buzzboxes a lo largo de la salvaje costa de Costa Oscura. Mientras que los elfos de la noche de Auberdine prefieren vivir en armonía con la naturaleza y apoyarse en antiguas costumbres, Maniveo Zumbang representa la curiosa y manitas presencia de la Alianza. Aposentado en la planta superior de la posada de Auberdine, rodeado de herramientas y piezas de repuesto, Maniveo apenas presta atención a las solemnes tradiciones druídicas de Kalimdor, centrándose en su lugar en desafíos mecánicos pragmáticos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Engineering"]="Wizbang's reliance on custom tools like gaffer jacks and electropellers highlights the classic gnomish mindset: mechanical answers to logistical problems in uncharted lands.",["race:Gnome"]="Seeing a fellow gnome operating an experimental communication network along Kalimdor's rugged coast is a welcome reminder of Gnomeregan's relentless inventiveness.",["race:NightElf"]="While elven sentinels and druids rely on whisps, messengers, and natural bonds, Wizbang brings loud, whirring gears and metal boxes into Darkshore's sacred woods."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Wizbang is located on the upper floor of the inn in the seaside night elf settlement of Auberdine, in Darkshore.",["al"]={"wizbang location","where is wizbang","auberdine gnome location"},["q"]="Where can I find Wizbang Cranktoggle?"},{["a"]="He is an Alliance engineer working on establishing and maintaining a network of automated communication machines called buzzboxes throughout the Darkshore wilderness.",["al"]={"why is wizbang in auberdine","wizbang purpose","what does wizbang do"},["q"]="What is Wizbang Cranktoggle doing in Darkshore?"},{["a"]="Buzzboxes are mechanical communication and monitoring devices invented by Wizbang Cranktoggle to relay information across Darkshore, though they frequently break down due to wildlife attacks and harsh weather.",["al"]={"what is a buzzbox","buzzbox lore","buzzbox purpose"},["q"]="What are buzzboxes?"},{["a"]="He shares a surname with Delber Cranktoggle, suggesting they may belong to the same family of tinkerers.",["al"]={"cranktoggle family","who is delber cranktoggle","wizbang relatives"},["q"]="Is Wizbang related to any other gnomes?"},{["a"]="As fellow members of the Grand Alliance, the night elves provide lodging and refuge to allied races in Auberdine, even if gnomish contraptions contrast sharply with traditional elven harmony.",["al"]={"night elves and gnomes","why allow engineering in auberdine"},["q"]="Why do the night elves tolerate his tinkering in Auberdine?"},{["a"]="Wizbang asks adventurers to help repair and configure his buzzbox machines, which involves scouring the shoreline for specialized parts like electropellers and gaffer jacks.",["al"]={"wizbang quests","what quests does wizbang offer"},["q"]="What tasks does Wizbang give to adventurers?"}},["kw"]={"auberdine","buzzbox","cranktoggle","darkshore","electropellers","engineer","gaffer jacks","gnome","wizbang"},["n"]="Wizbang Cranktoggle",["s"]="Wizbang Cranktoggle is an eccentric gnome engineer residing on the upper floor of the Auberdine inn. Despite being far from the cog-filled halls of Gnomeregan or Ironforge, he has turned his mechanical ingenuity toward setting up and maintaining automated communication devices known as buzzboxes across the wild coast of Darkshore.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While the night elves of Auberdine prefer living in harmony with nature and leaning upon ancient customs, Wizbang Cranktoggle represents the curious, tinkering presence of the Alliance. Perched on the top floor of Auberdine's inn, surrounded by tools and spare components, Wizbang pays little mind to the solemn druidic traditions of Kalimdor, focusing instead on pragmatic mechanical challenges.",["t"]="An Engineer in Auberdine"},{["b"]="Wizbang's primary project along Darkshore is deploying and maintaining his peculiar invention: the buzzbox. Designed to establish automated reporting and long-distance communication across the rugged, sprawling coastline, these contraptions often suffer from coastal weathering and the hostility of local wildlife. Wizbang frequently recruits travelers to gather components, salvage tools like gaffer jacks, and recover electropellers to keep his mechanical surveillance functioning.",["t"]="The Buzzbox Network"}}}}}
t["npc:yaw-sharpmane"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,216,21.311.0,18.309.0,21.179.0,31.100.0,38.159.0,27.165.0,52.178.0,45.148.0",["h"]="96c0c8",["n"]="Guin Crinafilada",["s"]="Guin Crinafilada. Guin Crinafilada es un experimentado instructor de cazadores tauren ubicado en el Poblado Pezuña de Sangre, en Mulgore. Guía a los jóvenes cazadores que parten del Campamento Narache, ayudándoles a dominar a las bestias salvajes de sus llanuras ancestrales. Situado entre las tiendas y hogueras del Poblado Pezuña de Sangre, Guin Crinafilada sirve a los Shu'halo como instructor en las artes de la puntería, el rastreo y la supervivencia. Los jóvenes cazadores que han demostrado su valía en la Mesa de la Nube Roja son enviados ante Guin para perfeccionar su destreza mientras se adentran en las amplias llanuras de Mulgore.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="For tauren hunters leaving the safety of Red Cloud Mesa, Yaw Sharpmane is an essential mentor who guides you through bonding with your very first wild companion.",["race:Tauren"]="Yaw represents the revered Shu'halo tradition of living in harmony with nature and honoring the spirits of the wild beasts of Mulgore."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Yaw Sharpmane is the resident hunter trainer in Bloodhoof Village. He instructs young tauren hunters in marksmanship, wilderness survival, and the art of taming animal companions.",["al"]={"yaw sharpmane","who is yaw","bloodhoof hunter trainer"},["q"]="Who is Yaw Sharpmane?"},{["a"]="Yaw is located in Bloodhoof Village, situated in central Mulgore along the shores of Stonebull Lake.",["al"]={"yaw sharpmane location","where is yaw","yaw coords"},["q"]="Where can I find Yaw Sharpmane?"},{["a"]="He offers standard hunter training, selling rank-ups for basic abilities and directing promising hunters through the rites required to tame and command beasts.",["al"]={"what does yaw teach","yaw hunter skills","yaw abilities"},["q"]="What does Yaw Sharpmane teach hunters?"},{["a"]="Yaw provides the tauren version of the beast-taming questline, starting with 'The Hunter's Path' and progressing through 'Taming the Beast' and 'Training the Beast.'",["al"]={"yaw quests","yaw sharpmane quests"},["q"]="What quests does Yaw offer?"},{["a"]="Upon reaching their tenth season, hunters are sent to Yaw to learn the sacred methods of capturing, feeding, and commanding permanent animal companions from the wilds of Mulgore.",["al"]={"yaw level 10","tame beast bloodhoof"},["q"]="Why do hunters need to speak to him around level 10?"},{["a"]="He will speak politely with travelers of other callings, but his professional knowledge and specific quest trials are reserved strictly for hunters.",["al"]={"yaw non hunters","can other classes talk to yaw"},["q"]="Does Yaw Sharpmane interact with non-hunters?"}},["kw"]={"beasts","bloodhoof","hunter","mulgore","sharpmane","taming","tauren","trainer","yaw"},["n"]="Yaw Sharpmane",["s"]="Yaw Sharpmane is an experienced tauren hunter trainer stationed in Bloodhoof Village in Mulgore. He guides young hunters venturing out from Camp Narache, helping them master the wild beasts of their ancestral plains.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Positioned amidst the tents and fires of Bloodhoof Village, Yaw Sharpmane serves the Shu'halo as an instructor in the ways of marksmanship, tracking, and survival. Young hunters who have proven themselves in Red Cloud Mesa are directed to Yaw to hone their craft as they step onto the broader plains of Mulgore.",["t"]="A Guide on the Plains"},{["b"]="Yaw's most essential role is guiding novice hunters through the ancient rite of taming wild beasts. He tasks initiates with bonding with the native fauna of Mulgore, testing their patience and respect for the natural balance before instructing them on how to properly care for and train a permanent companion.",["t"]="Mastering the Bond"}}}}}
t["subzone:addle-s-stead"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,242,21.445.0,35.406.1,31.134.0,37.166.0,26.177.0,50.180.1",["h"]="6966ed",["n"]="Granja de Addle",["s"]="Granja de Addle. Granja de Addle es una granja abandonada en el suroeste de Bosque del Ocaso, que yace en silencio bajo la penumbra del bosque al sur de Cerro del Cuervo. Aunque sus colonos originales huyeron hace mucho tiempo, la granja se ha convertido en un punto de reunión oculto para la Hermandad Defias. Al igual que muchos de los hogares olvidados repartidos por Bosque del Ocaso, Granja de Addle cayó en el abandono cuando la oscuridad y la ruina envolvieron la región. En lugar de permanecer vacía, la granja ha sido reutilizada por la Hermandad Defias. Sus agentes merodean por el perímetro, acechan dentro de la decrépita granja y esconden suministros en el establo, aprovechando el cobijo sombrío del suroeste de Bosque del Ocaso para pasar desapercibidos tanto para Guardia Nocturna como para las autoridades de Ventormenta.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,1},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="The covert outpost shows how deeply the Defias syndicates slip unnoticed across territorial borders, embedding their operatives behind the veil of Duskwood's gloom.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance investigators tracking the missing King Varian Wrynn, this dilapidated farmhouse holds vital conspiratorial dockets left by the Defias Brotherhood."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Addle's Stead is in southwestern Duskwood, situated just south of the Raven Hill township and directly west of the Vul'Gol Ogre Mound.",["al"]={"addle's stead location","where is addles stead","find addles stead"},["q"]="Where is Addle's Stead located?"},{["a"]="The farmstead is heavily occupied by the Defias Brotherhood, including night runners, night blades, and enchanters who use the old house and barn as a remote hideout.",["al"]={"who is at addles stead","mobs at addles stead","addles stead enemies"},["q"]="Who controls Addle's Stead right now?"},{["a"]="Like much of Duskwood, the farm was abandoned by its original inhabitants when the forest fell under a pervasive curse of darkness, beasts, and undead, driving common folk away.",["al"]={"what happened to the farm","who was addle","why is addles stead ruined"},["q"]="Why is the farm abandoned?"},{["a"]="Adventurers investigating the disappearance of King Varian Wrynn are guided toward Addle's Stead to retrieve an important Defias docket linking rogue agents to the royal abduction.",["al"]={"why go to addles stead","addles stead quest","missing king duskwood"},["q"]="What brings Alliance adventurers to Addle's Stead?"}},["kw"]={"addle's stead","addles stead","defias","defias brotherhood","duskwood","raven hill"},["n"]="Addle's Stead",["s"]="Addle's Stead is an abandoned farmstead in southwestern Duskwood, lying quiet under the forest's gloom south of Raven Hill. While its original homesteaders fled long ago, the farm has become a hidden staging ground for the Defias Brotherhood.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Like many of the forgotten homesteads scattered across Duskwood, Addle's Stead fell into disrepair when darkness and ruin enveloped the region. Rather than remaining empty, the farm has been repurposed by the Defias Brotherhood. Agents prowl the perimeter, lurk within the decrepit farmhouse, and stash supplies in the barn, using the shadowy cover of southwestern Duskwood to escape the notice of both the Night Watch and Stormwind authorities.",["t"]="A Outpost in the Dark"},{["b"]="The presence of the Defias here goes beyond simple banditry. Addle's Stead functions as an operational safehouse holding sensitive records for the Brotherhood. Crucial documents and dockets linking regional conspirators to the disappearance of King Varian Wrynn can be traced back to this very plot of land, turning an unassuming derelict farm into a vital thread in unraveling treason within the Alliance.",["t"]="Tangled in the King's Disappearance"}}}}}
t["subzone:agama-gor"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,311,24.479.0,22.458.0,18.164.0,49.247.0,31.194.0,56.247.0",["h"]="7d9a97",["n"]="Agama'gor",["s"]="Agama'gor. Agama'gor es un importante campamento de jabaespines Erizacrin situado en el sur de Los Baldíos, ubicado justo al norte del camino que lleva al oeste hacia Mulgore desde el Campamento Taurajo. Representa una espina clavada constante en el costado del cercano puesto avanzado de la Horda, rebosante de jabaespines hostiles que se aferran ferozmente a su escarpado territorio. Extendido a lo largo de las polvorientas llanuras del sur de Los Baldíos, Agama'gor sirve como un asentamiento fortificado para la agresiva tribu Erizacrin de jabaespines. Ubicados peligrosamente cerca del Campamento Taurajo, los jabaespines de aquí mantienen una densa red de zarzales, chozas y tótems rudimentarios. Su densa presencia supone una amenaza activa para los viajeros que se desplazan entre Los Baldíos y las verdes colinas de Mulgore, lo que empuja a los exploradores y cazadores de la Horda a librar una guerra constante de contención contra ellos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Camp Taurajo's safety hinges on keeping the Bristlebacks of Agama'gor in check, making the eradication of their warriors a priority for passing Horde defenders.",["race:Tauren"]="Situated directly on the path to the Great Gate and Mulgore, Agama'gor's marauders present an enduring danger to tauren supply lines and pilgrims."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Agama'gor is a large Bristleback quilboar settlement in the southern Barrens. It sits directly north of the main road heading west from Camp Taurajo toward Mulgore.",["al"]={"agamagor overview","what is this quilboar place","quilboar camp near taurajo"},["q"]="What is Agama'gor?"},{["a"]="Quilboar believe that all land touched by the fallen Ancient boar god Agamaggan rightfully belongs to them. As a result, the Bristlebacks regard the nearby tauren and orcs of Camp Taurajo as unwelcome invaders infringing upon their ancestral soil.",["al"]={"why do quilboar attack","quilboar hostility","why are bristlebacks angry"},["q"]="Why are the Bristleback quilboar here so hostile?"},{["a"]="The Bristleback quilboar throughout Agama'gor frequently carry Blood Shards—crystallized deposits steeped in primal power that can be traded to the exiled quilboar Mangletooth in Camp Taurajo.",["al"]={"what to get here","agamagor drops","why kill bristlebacks here"},["q"]="What can you find in Agama'gor?"},{["a"]="Mangletooth is an exiled quilboar held in a cage at Camp Taurajo. He harbors bitter grudges against his kin and will readily empower Horde adventurers with protective charms in exchange for Blood Shards taken from his former brethren in Agama'gor.",["al"]={"mangletooth connection","who is mangletooth","pig prisoner taurajo"},["q"]="Who is Mangletooth and how does he relate to this place?"}},["kw"]={"agama'gor","agamagor","barrens","blood shards","bristleback","camp taurajo","mangletooth","quilboar"},["n"]="Agama'gor",["s"]="Agama'gor is a major Bristleback quilboar encampment situated in the southern Barrens, nestled just north of the road leading west toward Mulgore from Camp Taurajo. It represents a constant thorn in the side of the nearby Horde outpost, teeming with hostile quilboar fiercely clinging to their rugged territory.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Sprawling across the dusty plains of the southern Barrens, Agama'gor serves as a fortified settlement for the aggressive Bristleback tribe of quilboar. Located dangerously close to Camp Taurajo, the quilboar here maintain a dense network of brambles, huts, and crude totems. Their heavy presence poses an active threat to travelers moving between the Barrens and the grassy hills of Mulgore, prompting Horde scouts and hunters to wage a perpetual war of containment against them.",["t"]="A Bristleback Stronghold"},{["b"]="Beyond the general animosity between the Horde and the quilboar, Agama'gor is a prime source of the mysterious, crimson stones known as Blood Shards. Found on the Bristleback inhabiting this village, these geomantic minerals are prized by Mangletooth, a quilboar exile held captive at Camp Taurajo. Driven by ancient beliefs tied to Agamaggan's sacred essence, adventurers often raid Agama'gor to harvest these shards and trade them for potent tribal charms.",["t"]="Blood Shards and Exile"}}}}}
t["subzone:agamand-family-crypt"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,295,18.535.0,42.109.0,33.129.0,39.175.0,57.144.0",["h"]="e7ccc6",["n"]="Cripta de la Familia Agamand",["s"]="Cripta de la Familia Agamand. Enclavada en las colinas justo al norte de los Molinos de Agamand, la Cripta de la Familia Agamand es el antiguo lugar de descanso de una de las dinastías agrícolas más ricas de Tirisfal. Ahora reclamada por la Plaga bajo el mando del capitán Dargol, sus tumbas han sido profanadas y sus antepasados durmientes han sido alzados como terrores descerebrados. Antes de la Tercera Guerra, la familia Agamand poseía extensas fincas por todo el norte de los Claros de Tirisfal, sepultando a sus antepasados dentro de este mausoleo en la ladera. Cuando la Plaga arruinó el reino, la cripta cayó en las garras del capitán Dargol, un agente de la Plaga. En lugar de dejar descansar en paz al acaudalado linaje, Dargol recurrió a la nigromancia oscura para despertar a los esqueletos sepultados y a apariciones vengativas, transformando un camposanto sagrado en un agresivo bastión de la Plaga justo en el límite del territorio de los Renegados.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Captain Dargol's occupation of the crypt is an intolerable Scourge presence in Tirisfal, mocking the dead and threatening the Undercity's northern frontier."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The crypt is carved into the hillside just north of Agamand Mills in the northern reaches of Tirisfal Glades.",["al"]={"agamand crypt location","where is the crypt","how to find agamand crypt"},["q"]="Where is the Agamand Family Crypt located?"},{["a"]="The tomb is held by Captain Dargol, a servant of the Scourge who orchestrates the dark magic within and commands the raised dead.",["al"]={"who is in agamand crypt","crypt boss","captain dargol"},["q"]="Who controls the crypt right now?"},{["a"]="The crypt is filled with awakened skeletons and restless spirits of the Agamand ancestors. Driven by dark magic, these vengeful undead assault anyone who steps into the tombs.",["al"]={"crypt enemies","what is inside agamand crypt","agamand crypt mobs"},["q"]="What will I encounter inside the crypt?"},{["a"]="No. The creatures inside are thralls of the Scourge answering to Captain Dargol, making them hostile to the Forsaken and living travelers alike.",["al"]={"are they forsaken","agamand crypt friendly","why attack undead"},["q"]="Are the undead inside the crypt allied with the Forsaken?"}},["kw"]={"agamand family crypt","agamand mills","captain dargol","crypt","mausoleum","scourge","skeletons","tirisfal glades"},["n"]="Agamand Family Crypt",["s"]="Tucked into the hills just north of Agamand Mills, the Agamand Family Crypt is the ancient resting ground of one of Tirisfal's wealthiest farming dynasties. Now claimed by the Scourge under Captain Dargol, its tombs have been ripped open, and the slumbering ancestors raised as mindless terrors.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War, the Agamand family held expansive estates across northern Tirisfal Glades, entombing their forebears within this hillside mausoleum. When the Plague brought ruin to the kingdom, the crypt fell into the clutches of Captain Dargol, an agent of the Scourge. Rather than letting the wealthy lineage rest in peace, Dargol employed dark necromancy to awaken the entombed skeletons and vengeful apparitions, transforming a sacred burial ground into an aggressive Scourge foothold right on the edge of Forsaken territory.",["t"]="Restless Ancestors"}}}}}
t["subzone:agamand-mills"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,244,15.662.0,16.563.0,42.290.0,33.222.0,42.218.0,27.266.0",["h"]="85a2d2",["n"]="Molinos de Agamand",["s"]="Molinos de Agamand. Molinos de Agamand es un extenso complejo de granjas y molinos ubicado en las colinas septentrionales de los Claros de Tirisfal. En su día fue la orgullosa hacienda de la acaudalada dinastía Agamand, pero ha caído en la ruina y se alza como la mayor fortaleza de la Plaga en la región. Hace siglos, ricos nobles inmigrantes de Strom establecieron la hacienda Agamand y construyeron una vasta red de molinos por el norte de Tirisfal. Cuando estalló la Tercera Guerra y la Plaga asoló Lordaeron, el patriarca Gregor Agamand se negó a huir: fortificó el recinto y convenció a sus sirvientes y trabajadores para que resistieran. Sus provisiones y muros de piedra podrían haber aguantado, pero su hijo menor, Devlin Agamand, traicionó a su propia sangre. Devlin asesinó a los guardias de la hacienda y dejó entrar a los muertos vivientes en los dormitorios. Debilitados desde dentro, los defensores restantes fueron aniquilados y la familia pasó a engrosar las filas de los no-muertos sin voluntad.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, reclaiming Agamand Mills is not merely tactical—it is personal vengeance against the Scourge and a settling of scores by former estate servants like Coleman Farthing."},["faq"]={{["a"]="When the Scourge ravaged Lordaeron, the Agamand family fortified their estate and attempted to hold out against the undead horde. However, the youngest son, Devlin Agamand, betrayed his family and opened the gates to the Scourge, leading to the slaughter and reanimation of everyone within.",["al"]={"what happened to agamand mills","why are there undead at the mills","agamand mills lore"},["q"]="Why is Agamand Mills overrun with Scourge?"},{["a"]="The estate serves as a regional forward outpost for the Scourge, led by Captain Dargol. Dargol operates deep within the fortified Agamand Family Crypt, where he uses dark magic to raise ancestral corpses into new soldiers.",["al"]={"who leads agamand mills","scourge leader tirisfal","who is in charge at the mills"},["q"]="Who controls the mills right now?"},{["a"]="The mills represent the largest concentration of mindless Scourge forces remaining in Tirisfal Glades. If left unchecked, Captain Dargol's force threatens Brill and could choke off roads leading south to the Undercity.",["al"]={"why brill attacks agamand","forsaken interest in agamand mills"},["q"]="Why do the Forsaken care about this place?"},{["a"]="They were an ancient, wealthy human noble house descended from Stromgarde immigrants who purchased rich farmlands in Tirisfal over a millennium ago. Today, its reanimated scions—including Gregor, Nissa, Thurman, and Devlin—wander the grounds as mindless thralls.",["al"]={"who are the agamands","agamand lineage","gregor agamand"},["q"]="Who was the Agamand family?"}},["kw"]={"agamand","agamand family crypt","agamand mills","captain dargol","devlin agamand","gregor agamand","scourge","tirisfal glades"},["n"]="Agamand Mills",["s"]="Agamand Mills is a sprawling farm and windmill complex nestled in the northern heights of Tirisfal Glades. Once the proud estate of the wealthy Agamand dynasty, it has fallen into ruin and stands as the largest Scourge stronghold in the region.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Centuries ago, wealthy noble immigrants from Strom established the Agamand estate, building a vast milling network across northern Tirisfal. When the Third War broke out and the Scourge swept across Lordaeron, the patriarch Gregor Agamand refused to flee, fortifying the compound and convincing his retainers and laborers to make their stand. Their provisions and stone walls might have held, but their youngest son, Devlin Agamand, betrayed his blood. Devlin slaughtered the estate watchmen and let the walking dead into the sleeping quarters. Crippled from within, the remaining defenders were wiped out, and the family joined the mindless ranks of the undead.",["t"]="A House Divided"},{["b"]="Today, the Agamand Mills are the most entrenched bastion of the Scourge in Tirisfal Glades, posing an immediate threat to the Forsaken realm. The rotting windmills now churn above infested fields of wights, zombies, and skeletal horrors. Beneath the estate, Captain Dargol commands the garrison from the deep Agamand Family Crypt, practicing necromancy to reanimate generations of Agamand ancestors. From Brill, Magistrate Sevren and the Deathguards wage an active campaign to clear the mills and purge the Scourge presence before it can march upon the Undercity.",["t"]="A Bastion of Rot"}}}}}
t["subzone:aldrassil"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,254,19.549.0,18.215.0,38.156.0,32.205.0",["h"]="672674",["n"]="Aldrassil",["s"]="Aldrassil. Aldrassil es el colosal árbol y asentamiento situado en el corazón de Cañada Umbría, en el noreste de Teldrassil. Sirve como refugio principal y campo de entrenamiento para los jóvenes kaldorei, y sus huecos tallados albergan instructores, comerciantes y líderes locales. Elevándose por encima del apartado valle de Cañada Umbría, Aldrassil funciona tanto de refugio como de centro cívico para los jóvenes elfos de la noche que dan sus primeros pasos en el mundo. Construidas dentro y alrededor del colosal tronco de este antiguo árbol, unas rampas serpenteantes pasan junto a instructores de clase y artesanos hasta el alto nido donde Tenaron Tormentagarre supervisa la protección del claro. Mientras la rama del mundo, Teldrassil, se extiende por el horizonte, Aldrassil proporciona un dosel seguro y firme donde los novicios aprenden sus artes antes de aventurarse hacia las turbulentas tierras salvajes de Kalimdor.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Aldrassil demonstrates the kaldorei affinity for living architecture, shaped from living wood without breaking the balance of the forest.",["race:NightElf"]="For many young kaldorei, the carved hollows and ramps of Aldrassil are their first memory of civic life and the foundation of their early training."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Aldrassil is the massive, hollowed-out tree and settlement situated in the center of Shadowglen, northeastern Teldrassil. It serves as the starting haven where young night elves gather training, goods, and guidance.",["al"]={"aldrassil tree","what is aldrassil","shadowglen big tree"},["q"]="What is Aldrassil?"},{["a"]="Tenaron Stormgrip oversees Shadowglen from his roost at the very top of Aldrassil, coordinating the defense of the vale and guiding newly awakened kaldorei.",["al"]={"who leads aldrassil","aldrassil leader","tenaron stormgrip location"},["q"]="Who leads the settlement at Aldrassil?"},{["a"]="The tree houses class trainers for young night elf warriors, rogues, druids, hunters, and priests, alongside local supply merchants, armorers, and questgivers attending to the immediate needs of the glade.",["al"]={"trainers in aldrassil","vendors aldrassil","what is in aldrassil"},["q"]="What services can be found here?"}},["kw"]={"aldrassil","great tree","kaldorei","night elf starting","shadowglen","teldrassil","tenaron stormgrip"},["n"]="Aldrassil",["s"]="Aldrassil is the colossal bough-tree and settlement nestled at the heart of Shadowglen in northeastern Teldrassil. Serving as the primary refuge and training ground for young kaldorei, its carved hollows shelter trainers, merchants, and local leadership.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Rising high above the secluded vale of Shadowglen, Aldrassil functions as both shelter and civic hub for young night elves taking their first steps in the world. Built into and around the colossal trunk of this ancient growth, winding ramps lead past class trainers and artisans to the high roost where Tenaron Stormgrip oversees the glade's protection. While the world bough Teldrassil stretches across the horizon, Aldrassil provides a safe, grounded canopy where novices learn their arts before venturing down into the troubled wilds of Kalimdor.",["t"]="Heart of Shadowglen"}}}}}
t["subzone:alexston-farmstead"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,240,18.427.0,12.388.0,32.191.0,26.216.0,52.246.0,46.182.0",["h"]="af5622",["n"]="Hacienda de Alexston",["s"]="Hacienda de Alexston. La Hacienda de Alexston es una granja abandonada en los Páramos de Poniente, cubierta de maleza y acechada por Vigías de la cosecha fuera de control. En su día fue el hogar de la infancia del arquitecto municipal de Ventormenta, Baros Alexston, pero ha acabado en la ruina como gran parte del granero que la rodea. Situada en medio de las secas llanuras de los Páramos de Poniente, la Hacienda de Alexston se alza como otro sombrío testimonio del abandono del reino. Al igual que las fincas vecinas, la granja fue abandonada por sus cuidadores cuando el bandidaje estalló por toda la comarca. Hoy en día, los campos están cubiertos de maleza y los Vigías de la cosecha mecánicos que quedaron atrás para cuidar los cultivos se han descontrolado, atacando violentamente a cualquiera que se acerque a la yerma casa de campo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The farm is a reminder of the quiet, hardworking roots that built Stormwind's finest minds, as well as the Alliance's ongoing struggle to protect its own borders."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The farmstead takes its name from the family of Baros Alexston, the city architect of Stormwind. Baros worked the land here as a young boy before moving to the capital to pursue architecture.",["al"]={"who owns this farm","alexston owner","whose farm is this"},["q"]="Who owns the Alexston Farmstead?"},{["a"]="Like much of Westfall, the farmstead was abandoned in the wake of widespread unrest and banditry by the Defias Brotherhood. With the kingdom unable to offer protection, the farmers fled, leaving the homestead to rot.",["al"]={"why abandoned","what happened to alexston farm","who ruined the farm"},["q"]="Why is the farm abandoned?"},{["a"]="The mechanical Harvest Watchers were originally built to work the soil and protect crops from scavengers. Left unmaintained after the farmers fled, their internal clockwork has malfunctioned, turning them violently hostile to any living creature.",["al"]={"why harvest watchers attack","hostile scarecrows","harvest golems hostile"},["q"]="Why are mechanical scarecrows attacking people here?"},{["a"]="Baros Alexston left behind a personal compass in the farmhouse from his youth. Travelers doing work in Stormwind City are sometimes asked to retrieve it from the abandoned homestead.",["al"]={"quest here","loot in farm","baros item"},["q"]="Is there anything hidden inside the farmhouse?"}},["kw"]={"alexston","architect","baros","compass","farmstead","harvest watcher","westfall"},["n"]="Alexston Farmstead",["s"]="The Alexston Farmstead is a derelict farm in Westfall, overgrown and prowled by haywire Harvest Watchers. Once the childhood home of Stormwind's city architect, Baros Alexston, it has fallen into ruin like much of the breadbasket around it.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated amidst the dry plains of Westfall, the Alexston Farmstead stands as another grim testament to the kingdom's neglect. Like neighboring estates, the farm was abandoned by its caretakers when banditry erupted across the countryside. Today, the fields are overgrown, and the mechanical Harvest Watchers left behind to tend the crops have spun out of control, violently attacking anyone who approaches the barren farmhouse.",["t"]="A Fallen Homestead"},{["b"]="Despite its bleak state, the farm is tied to one of Stormwind's most prominent citizens. Baros Alexston, the skilled architect who helped design parts of the rebuilt capital, spent his youth toiling on these very fields. He left the farmstead long before the unrest began to pursue his trade in masonry and construction, leaving behind a memento of his early life nestled among the ruins.",["t"]="Humble Roots"}}}}}
t["subzone:algaz-station"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,284,26.539.0,22.180.0,36.153.0,34.178.0",["h"]="5ffc90",["n"]="Estación de Algaz",["s"]="Estación de Algaz. La Estación de Algaz es un puesto de avanzada militar enano situado en el noroeste de Loch Modan, directamente al sur del paso fortificado de Dun Algaz. Al guarnecer el acceso a los túneles del norte, su destacamento de montaraces ayuda a proteger a los viajeros y vigilar la frontera que conduce hacia Los Humedales. Ubicada justo al este del Paso de la Puerta Norte y al sur de Dun Algaz, la Estación de Algaz sirve como un punto de vigilancia estratégico vital para el reino de Forjaz. Un cuadro de montaraces enanos mantiene aquí una vigilia permanente, manteniendo el camino vital entre Loch Modan y las tierras bajas del norte abierto al comercio y al movimiento de tropas. Dadas las frecuentes amenazas en las colinas circundantes, desde bestias errantes hasta troggs invasores, el puesto de avanzada proporciona descanso, reparaciones y apoyo marcial para los viajeros fatigados antes de que se aventuren a través de los túneles de las montañas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The outpost offers a secure staging ground and repair stop for Alliance adventurers journeying between Loch Modan and the marshlands of the north.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarven travelers, Algaz Station is a familiar emblem of Ironforge's reach, ensuring the king's highways remain guarded against threats spilling from the mountains."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is an Ironforge military outpost in northwestern Loch Modan. It serves as a guard post and waystation for Mountaineers patrolling the mountain passes leading north to Dun Algaz.",["al"]={"what is this place","algaz station purpose","who runs algaz station"},["q"]="What is Algaz Station?"},{["a"]="It takes its name from Dun Algaz, the massive dwarven pass and tunnel system situated just north of the station that connects Loch Modan to the Wetlands.",["al"]={"why is it called algaz station","dun algaz connection","name meaning"},["q"]="Where does the station get its name?"},{["a"]="The outpost is manned by dwarven Mountaineers, including Mountaineer Stormpike, alongside support personnel like the armorer Gothor Brumn who provides field repairs to travelers.",["al"]={"who is here","npcs at algaz station","mountaineer stormpike location"},["q"]="Who can be found at Algaz Station?"}},["kw"]={"algaz station","dun algaz","gothor brumn","ironforge","loch modan","mountaineer stormpike","mountaineers","north gate pass"},["n"]="Algaz Station",["s"]="Algaz Station is a dwarven military outpost situated in northwestern Loch Modan, directly south of the fortified pass of Dun Algaz. Manning the approach to the northern tunnels, its garrison of Mountaineers helps safeguard travelers and watch the frontier leading toward the Wetlands.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched just east of North Gate Pass and south of Dun Algaz, Algaz Station serves as a vital strategic watchpoint for the kingdom of Ironforge. A cadre of dwarven Mountaineers maintains a permanent vigil here, keeping the vital road between Loch Modan and the northern lowlands open to trade and troop movements. Given the frequent threats in the surrounding hills, from wandering beasts to encroaching troggs, the outpost provides respite, repairs, and martial support for weary travelers before they venture through the mountain tunnels.",["t"]="Watching the Northern Pass"}}}}}
t["subzone:alterac-mountains"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,274,14.492.0,22.502.0,42.266.0,24.302.0,43.246.0,36.195.0",["h"]="5d8f44",["n"]="Montañas de Alterac",["s"]="Montañas de Alterac. Las Montañas de Alterac son una cordillera escarpada y cubierta de nieve que se alza justo sobre los ondulados pastos de Trabalomas. Antaño el corazón de un orgulloso reino humano, sus laderas albergan ahora asentamientos en ruinas, facciones de bandidos y una naturaleza salvaje y peligrosa donde los viajeros rara vez se adentran desprotegidos. Mucho antes de que las colinas cayeran en el caos, estas tierras altas formaban la nación soberana de Alterac, uno de los siete reinos nacidos del antiguo Arathor. Ese legado se quebró durante la Segunda Guerra, cuando el rey Aiden Perenolde forjó un pacto clandestino con la Horda Antigua, permitiendo a las fuerzas orcas atravesar los picos a cambio de la seguridad de su reino. La Alianza de Lordaeron descubrió la traición y depuso a Perenolde, dejando la región fracturada por la ley marcial y disputas territoriales.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="The mountain passes are rife with Syndicate agents and hired cutthroats, making the hills a prime testing ground for survival and counter-espionage.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Alterac stands as a bitter monument to betrayal, where Perenolde's treachery nearly doomed humanity during the Second War."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The human kingdom of Alterac held these mountains for generations after the splintering of the Empire of Arathor. Its capital sat among the highest peaks, commanding the roads between Lordaeron, Dalaran, and the Arathi highlands until its fall during the Second War.",["al"]={"who owned alterac","what was alterac","alterac kingdom lore"},["q"]="What kingdom used to rule these mountains?"},{["a"]="During the Second War, King Aiden Perenolde betrayed the Alliance of Lordaeron by assisting the Horde. When the treason was exposed, Alliance armies crushed Alterac's forces and deposed the crown. With no legitimate ruler and subsequent devastation from the Third War, the nation collapsed into rubble.",["al"]={"what happened to alterac","who destroyed alterac","ruins of alterac backstory"},["q"]="Why is Alterac in ruins?"},{["a"]="The Syndicate is an outlaw syndicate made up of former Alteraci nobility and their retainers. Led by Aliden Perenolde, they employ brigands, assassins, and rogue mercenaries to destabilize the region in hopes of violently restoring their kingdom.",["al"]={"who is the syndicate","what is the syndicate","why are there bandits in alterac"},["q"]="Who are the Syndicate lurking in the hills?"},{["a"]="Travelers brave enough to climb the slopes must contend with the brutal Crushridge ogres, packs of Highland gnolls, scavenging kobolds, and opportunistic Syndicate brigands patrolling the passes.",["al"]={"what lives in alterac","alterac monsters","threats in alterac"},["q"]="What threats wander the snowy peaks?"}},["kw"]={"alterac","crushridge","hillsbrad","mountains","perenolde","strahnbrad","syndicate"},["n"]="Alterac Mountains",["s"]="The Alterac Mountains are a rugged, snow-capped range rising directly above the rolling pastures of Hillsbrad. Once the heart of a proud human kingdom, the slopes now harbor ruined settlements, bandit factions, and dangerous wilderness where travelers rarely walk unguarded.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Long before the hills fell into chaos, these highlands formed the sovereign nation of Alterac, one of the seven kingdoms born from ancient Arathor. That legacy shattered during the Second War when King Aiden Perenolde struck a clandestine pact with the Old Horde, allowing orcish forces passage through the peaks in exchange for his kingdom's safety. The Alliance of Lordaeron uncovered the betrayal and deposed Perenolde, leaving the region fractured by martial law and territorial disputes.",["t"]="A Fallen Realm"},{["b"]="Following the devastation of the Third War, the mountains collapsed into complete lawlessness. The disinherited nobles of the realm banded together to form the Syndicate, operating out of the ruins of Strahnbrad and plotting to reclaim their lost dominion through sabotage and assassination. Between ruthless Crushridge ogres occupying the shattered capital, marauding gnolls, and the shattered magical ruins around Dalaran, the passes of Alterac remain some of the most perilous pathways in Lordaeron.",["t"]="Wilderness and Bandits"}}}}}
t["subzone:alther-s-mill"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,425,26.491.0,17.485.0,22.230.0,26.247.0,36.205.0,34.215.0",["h"]="dc8c4d",["n"]="Molino de Alther",["s"]="Molino de Alther. El Molino de Alther es un aserradero en ruinas enclavado en las escarpadas colinas al noreste de Villa del Lago, en las Montañas Crestagrana. Antaño una fuente vital de madera procesada para los constructores locales, sus terrenos abandonados se han deteriorado hasta convertirse en un refugio para carroñeros salvajes y depredadores al acecho. Para los aventureros que viajan al este hacia Petravista, estas estructuras ruinosas sirven como un sombrío punto de referencia que delimita el fin del territorio fronterizo seguro. Antes de que la región cayera presa de depredadores invasores y de las incursiones orcas, el Molino de Alther bullía con el comercio maderero que abastecía la construcción de Villa del Lago y los asentamientos circundantes. Su apacible claro al noreste del Lago Sempiterno ofrecía un fácil acceso a las masas forestales de las montañas. A medida que aumentaban las tensiones en el reino de Ventormenta y el Clan Roca Negra descendía desde las alturas de Petravista, los molineros locales abandonaron las instalaciones, dejando que los secos edificios de madera y la rueda se pudrieran con el tiempo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Alliance scoundrels know Alther's Mill well, as thieves' syndicates use the scattered, forgotten lockboxes and secluded grounds of the mill as a quiet training ground to practice delicate lockpicking.",["faction:Alliance"]="The ruined mill stands as another stark reminder of Stormwind's strained frontier garrisons, where valuable industry lies broken and abandoned within sight of Lakeshire."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Alther's Mill is a ruined lumber mill located northeast of Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains. It previously harvested and processed timber for the surrounding settlements until mounting wilderness dangers forced its abandonment.",["al"]={"alther's mill","althers mill","what is this place","what was alther's mill"},["q"]="What is Alther's Mill?"},{["a"]="As regional defenses weakened following the First and Second Wars, aggressive wildlife like giant spiders and encroachment by Blackrock orcs made frontier operations too perilous for ordinary laborers to maintain without royal military protection.",["al"]={"why abandoned","who abandoned althers mill","what happened to the millers"},["q"]="Why is the mill abandoned?"},{["a"]="The grounds and surrounding scrublands are primarily overrun by giant mountain tarantulas, scavenger buzzards, and roving predators, along with stray marauders moving between Stonewatch and Lake Everstill.",["al"]={"enemies at althers mill","creatures at mill","what lives here"},["q"]="What creatures roam around the mill?"},{["a"]="The isolated, debris-strewn grounds make it a favored proving ground for Alliance rogues, who are directed here by their trainers to practice picking locked footlockers and retrieve valuable thieving certifications.",["al"]={"rogue quest mill","althers mill lockpicking","thieving certificate"},["q"]="Why do rogues visit Alther's Mill?"}},["kw"]={"alther's mill","althers mill","lakeshire","lockpicking","lumber mill","redridge","spiders","stonewatch"},["n"]="Alther's Mill",["s"]="Alther's Mill is a ruined lumber mill tucked into the rugged hills northeast of Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains. Once a vital source of processed timber for local builders, the abandoned grounds have deteriorated into a haven for feral scavengers and prowling predators. For adventurers traveling east toward Stonewatch, the dilapidated structures serve as a grim landmark marking the boundary of safe frontier territory.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the region fell prey to invading predators and orc raids, Alther's Mill bustled with timber trade that supplied the construction of Lakeshire and surrounding settlements. Its quiet clearing northeast of Lake Everstill provided ready access to mountain timber stands. As turmoil mounted across the kingdom of Stormwind and the Blackrock clan pushed down from the heights of Stonewatch, local millers abandoned the facility, leaving the dry timber buildings and wheel to decay into rot.",["t"]="An Abandoned Frontier Mill"},{["b"]="In the absence of human workers, the mill became infested with monstrous tarantulas, carrion vultures, and opportunistic raiders. Travelers cutting through the path to the eastern passes must skirt its shadowed perimeter carefully. In recent years, shadowy operatives and thieves have also taken advantage of the abandoned compound, using its discarded storage boxes and hidden corners to hone illicit lockpicking crafts and covert trades far from the eyes of the Lakeshire Town Watch.",["t"]="Shadows and Scrap"}}}}}
t["subzone:amberstill-ranch"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,374,25.495.0,35.200.0,37.240.0,33.228.0,42.163.0",["h"]="54f00e",["n"]="Granja de Semperámbar",["s"]="Granja de Semperámbar. La Granja de Semperámbar es un tranquilo hogar enano enclavado junto al camino nevado hacia Loch Modan, directamente al norte de la Cantera de Gol'Bolar. Sirve como el principal centro de cría y adiestramiento de los célebres carneros de montaña de Forjaz. Los aventureros visitan la granja para adquirir resistentes monturas enanas, entrenar equitación o ayudar a la familia a defender su ganado de los depredadores locales. Resguardada contra los riscos de Dun Morogh, la Granja de Semperámbar es famosa en todo Khaz Modan por criar los carneros de montaña más robustos de los Reinos del Este. La familia Amberstill gestiona los establos y corrales, adiestrando a estas bestias de paso firme para sortear traicioneros pasos nevados y escarpados acantilados alpinos. Además de suministrar monturas y ganado doméstico, la familia a menudo lidia con la salvaje fauna de las colinas, en particular con los wéndigos errantes atraídos por el olor del rebaño fresco.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The sturdy rams raised by the Amberstills provide the Alliance with dependable, cold-weather cavalry suitable for rugged mountain terrain.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarven adventurers, the ranch is a proud cultural cornerstone where young heroes acquire their first Barak Tor'ol ram mount."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The ranch is the Alliance's central hub for breeding Barak Tor'ol mountain rams. Dwarves and honored Alliance champions come here to learn ram riding and purchase mounts from the local stable masters.",["al"]={"amberstill purpose","why visit amberstill","amberstill rams"},["q"]="What is Amberstill Ranch known for?"},{["a"]="Rams are traditionally reserved for dwarven riders who understand their stubborn temperament. Members of other Alliance races may only learn to ride and purchase them if they have earned the utmost trust and exalted standing with Ironforge.",["al"]={"buy rams non dwarf","human buy ram","ram mount requirements"},["q"]="Can non-dwarves purchase mounts here?"},{["a"]="The herd is under constant threat from hungry wendigos descending from the frozen bluffs. The most notorious predator prowling the surrounding heights is Vagash, a massive wendigo that regularly targets the vulnerable livestock.",["al"]={"amberstill danger","wendigo threat","vagash quest"},["q"]="What threats does the ranch face?"},{["a"]="Young Yarlyn Amberstill keeps a collection of domestic snowshoe rabbits and is willing to sell crated rabbits to travelers looking for a companion pet on the road.",["al"]={"amberstill rabbit","snowshoe rabbit pet","yarlyn amberstill"},["q"]="Can you obtain anything else at the ranch?"}},["kw"]={"amberstill","mount vendor","rams","ranch","riding trainer","snowshoe rabbit","vagash","yarlyn"},["n"]="Amberstill Ranch",["s"]="Amberstill Ranch is a tranquil dwarven homestead nestled along the snowy roadway toward Loch Modan, directly north of Gol'Bolar Quarry. It serves as the primary breeding and training grounds for Ironforge's celebrated mountain rams. Adventurers visit the ranch to acquire hardy dwarven mounts, train in riding, or help the family defend their livestock from local predators.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked against the crags of Dun Morogh, Amberstill Ranch is renowned throughout Khaz Modan for raising the sturdiest mountain rams in the Eastern Kingdoms. The Amberstill family manages the stables and paddocks, training these sure-footed beasts to navigate treacherous snowy passes and steep alpine cliffs. Outside of supplying riding mounts and domestic livestock, the family often contends with the savage fauna of the hills, particularly wandering wendigos drawn by the scent of fresh flock.",["t"]="Home of the Mountain Rams"}}}}}
t["subzone:ameth-aran"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,301,19.524.0,28.517.1,28.254.0,39.209.0,25.251.1,46.276.0",["h"]="69a8a5",["n"]="Ameth'Aran",["s"]="Ameth'Aran. Ameth'Aran es una antigua ruina en el sur de Costa Oscura, en su día una próspera ciudad donde los Altonato de la reina Azshara practicaban la hechicería arcana. Cuando el Gran Cataclismo destrozó el mundo antiguo, la ciudad cayó con él. Hoy en día, sus columnatas rotas están encantadas por los fantasmas vengativos de los elfos que murieron allí. Antes del Gran Cataclismo, Ameth'Aran y su asentamiento hermano, Bashal'Aran, se alzaban como centros gemelos de la influencia de los Altonato a lo largo de la antigua costa. Con el favor de la reina Azshara, la ciudad presumía de bulliciosos bazares y elegantes santuarios dedicados a Elune, aunque su nobleza gobernante se dedicaba a la experimentación arcana desenfrenada. Gobernada desde la distancia por el hechicero Athrikus Narassin en La torre de Althalaxx, la ciudad prosperó hasta que el colapso catastrófico del Pozo de la Eternidad desgarró el Imperio kaldorei.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,1,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids view the ruins as an unhealed scar upon Darkshore, where tormented spirits linger and disrupt the natural balance of the wilds.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Ameth'Aran is a grim monument to the hubris and treachery of the Highborne caste that brought about the Sundering."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Ameth'Aran was already in ruins in the final days of the Kaldorei Empire, and it was destroyed when the Well of Eternity was shattered in the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago. The ruins remain haunted by the spirits of the Highborne who died there.",["al"]={"why is ametharan ruined","ameth aran history","fall of ametharan"},["q"]="What happened to Ameth'Aran?"},{["a"]="They are the restless spirits of the Highborne elves who lived and practiced arcane magic in the city before the Great Sundering. Unable to find rest, they wander the broken stones in perpetual agony and fury.",["al"]={"ghosts in ameth aran","ametharan specters","highborne ghosts darkshore"},["q"]="Who are the ghosts wandering the ruins?"},{["a"]="Anaya Dawnrunner was a resident of Ameth'Aran and the beloved of Cerellean Whiteclaw. She perished when the city fell during the Sundering, and her ghost remained bound to the ruins until Cerellean sought outside aid to finally grant her soul release.",["al"]={"anaya dawnrunner","cerellean lover","ameth aran lost love"},["q"]="Who was Anaya Dawnrunner?"},{["a"]="The ruins contain ancient stone tablets inscribed with the history of Ameth'Aran and the account of its fall. Sentinel Tysha Moonblade attempted to decipher them to deliver a historical report to the Cenarion Circle, but hostile ghosts forced her to rely on passing travelers.",["al"]={"ametharan tablets","runestones in ameth aran","fall of ametharan tablets"},["q"]="What are the stone tablets found in the ruins?"}},["kw"]={"ameth'aran","anaya dawnrunner","athrikus narassin","bashal'aran","cerellean whiteclaw","darkshore","highborne","tysha moonblade"},["n"]="Ameth'Aran",["s"]="Ameth'Aran is an ancient ruin in southern Darkshore, once a thriving city where Queen Azshara's Highborne practiced arcane sorcery. When the Great Sundering shattered the ancient world, the city fell with it. Today, its broken colonnades are haunted by the vengeful ghosts of the elves who died there.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Great Sundering, Ameth'Aran and its sister settlement, Bashal'Aran, stood as twin centers of Highborne influence along the ancient coastline. Under the favor of Queen Azshara, the city boasted bustling bazaars and graceful shrines to Elune, though its ruling nobility dedicated themselves to unrestrained arcane experimentation. Governed from afar by the sorcerer Athrikus Narassin in the Tower of Althalaxx, the city thrived until the catastrophic collapse of the Well of Eternity tore the Kaldorei Empire apart.",["t"]="A City of Sorcerers"},{["b"]="As the world began to tear itself apart, Athrikus Narassin returned to Ameth'Aran, promising his panicked subjects salvation through powerful shielding magic. Instead of shielding them, the sorcerer enacted a horrific betrayal, stealing their life force to feed his own soul gems under the cruel guise of giving them eternal preservation. Shattered by cataclysm and dark magic, Ameth'Aran fell. Today, its grounds are stalked by anguished Highborne specters, unable to find rest ten thousand years after their murder.",["t"]="Betrayal and Eternal Torment"}}}}}
t["subzone:angerfang-encampment"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,284,21.531.0,19.554.1,35.252.0,45.277.0,52.249.0,41.191.0",["h"]="69e78e",["n"]="Campamento Dentellada",["s"]="Campamento Dentellada. El Campamento Dentellada es el principal bastión del clan Faucedraco en el centro de Los Pantanales. Liderados por el Jefe Nek'rosh Skullcrusher, estos orcos renegados utilizan el extenso campamento como base de operaciones para amenazar los asentamientos enanos cercanos y planear la destrucción del Puerto de Menethil. Extendido a lo largo del fango en el centro de Los Pantanales, el Campamento Dentellada sirve como el corazón fortificado del poder Faucedraco en la región. A diferencia de las partidas de asalto dispersas que deambulan por los pantanos, este recinto cuenta con barricadas fuertemente defendidas, torres de vigilancia y una formidable hueste de guerreros, custodios óseos y oscuros lanzadores de conjuros leales a las viejas costumbres. Desde aquí, los Faucedraco proyectan su fuerza militar por todos los pantanos, asaltando a los viajeros en los caminos y amenazando las excavaciones enanas cercanas, como la Excavación de Whelgar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="The dark shadowwarders within the encampment carry Rods of Channeling, essential artifacts sought for the bindings written within the Tome of the Cabal.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the defenders of Menethil Harbor, Angerfang is a clear and present danger; bringing down Nek'rosh's war banners and taking his head is vital to securing the coastal trade routes."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The camp is ruled by Chieftain Nek'rosh Skullcrusher, the son of the notorious Dragonmaw warlock Nekros Skullcrusher. From his command tent deep within the encampment, Nek'rosh directs regional raiding parties and plans the conquest of Menethil Harbor.",["al"]={"who leads angerfang","angerfang boss","who is in charge here","nekrosh camp"},["q"]="Who rules the Angerfang Encampment?"},{["a"]="No. The Dragonmaw clan here remains independent of Thrall's New Horde. They cling to the dark heritage of the Old Horde, remaining hostile to Alliance and Horde travelers alike. Thrall's warriors view them as feral outcasts, even hunting them down for armor crafting materials.",["al"]={"are dragonmaw horde","are angerfang friendly to horde","is angerfang part of thralls horde"},["q"]="Are the orcs here allied with Thrall's Horde?"},{["a"]="Captain Stoutfist and the dwarven defenders of Menethil Harbor discovered that Nek'rosh has assembled catapults and massive forces at Angerfang to bombard and conquer the harbor. The Alliance attacks preemptively to crush the siege before it begins.",["al"]={"why attack angerfang","captain stoutfist angerfang","why kill nekrosh"},["q"]="Why is the Alliance focused on destroying this camp?"},{["a"]="The dark spellcasters among the Dragonmaw at Angerfang carry Rods of Channeling, dark ritual implements coveted by practitioners of the demonic arts seeking to complete the Tome of the Cabal.",["al"]={"warlock quest angerfang","tome of the cabal wetlands","rod of channeling angerfang"},["q"]="Why do warlocks seek out this encampment?"}},["kw"]={"angerfang","dragonmaw","menethil","nek'rosh","skullcrusher","stoutfist","wetlands","whelgar"},["n"]="Angerfang Encampment",["s"]="The Angerfang Encampment is the primary stronghold of the Dragonmaw clan in the central Wetlands. Led by Chieftain Nek'rosh Skullcrusher, these renegade orcs use the sprawling camp as a staging ground to threaten nearby dwarven settlements and plot the destruction of Menethil Harbor.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Sprawling across the muck of the central Wetlands, the Angerfang Encampment serves as the fortified heart of Dragonmaw power in the region. Unlike the scattered raiding parties found wandering the marshes, this compound boasts heavily defended barricades, watchtowers, and a formidable host of warriors, bonewarders, and dark spellcasters loyal to the old ways. From here, the Dragonmaw project military force across the marshlands, raiding travelers along the roads and menacing nearby dwarven digs like Whelgar's Excavation Site.",["t"]="A Bastion in the Bogs"},{["b"]="The encampment is commanded by Chieftain Nek'rosh Skullcrusher, son of the infamous warlock Nekros who once enslaved the red dragonflight at Grim Batol. Harboring a deep hatred for the Alliance, Nek'rosh has marshaled catapults and raised war banners in preparation for an all-out assault against Menethil Harbor. Aware of the looming siege, Alliance commanders in the port city dispatch champions into the belly of Angerfang to capture their banners, smash their war machines, and claim Nek'rosh's head before his offensive can drown the harbor in fire.",["t"]="Nek'rosh's Ambition"}}}}}
t["subzone:apothecarium"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,415,18.603.0,26.285.0,34.255.0,27.202.0,54.199.0,35.144.0",["h"]="2aac4e",["n"]="Apothecarium",["s"]="Apothecarium. El Apothecarium es el barrio suroeste de Entrañas y la sede de la Sociedad Real de Boticarios. Dentro de estos nocivos laboratorios, los alquimistas Renegados trabajan incansablemente a las órdenes del Maestro boticario Faranell para elaborar pestes virulentas, toxinas y horrores modificados. Se erige como el lúgubre corazón de la investigación biológica de Entrañas, vital para la campaña de Lady Sylvanas contra los vivos y la Plaga. Ocupando la terraza suroeste de la capital subterránea, el Apothecarium es un laberinto de cubas burbujeantes, mesas de disección y acres vapores químicos. Liderada por el Maestro boticario Faranell, la Sociedad Real de Boticarios utiliza este distrito para profundizar en su comprensión de la mortalidad y la putrefacción. Aquí, alquimistas y cirujanos experimentan con injertos de tejido, vivisección y el ensamblaje de poderosas abominaciones. Su propósito primordial, encomendado por Lady Sylvanas Brisaveloz, es la formulación de una nueva peste capaz de erradicar tanto a la Plaga como a la persistente presencia humana en Lordaeron.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Herbalism"]="Botanists supply the foul distillers of the Royal Apothecary Society with rare, blighted flora gathered from the ruins of the northern kingdoms.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the Apothecarium is the forge of their survival, producing the chemical and stitched weapons essential to holding Lordaeron against overwhelming enemies."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Apothecarium serves as the research and manufacturing wing for the Royal Apothecary Society. It is where Forsaken alchemists brew experimental poisons, refine the New Plague, construct abominations, and instruct practitioners in alchemy and herbalism.",["al"]={"apothecarium purpose","what happens here","why does the apothecarium exist"},["q"]="What is the Apothecarium used for?"},{["a"]="The district and its researchers are led by Master Apothecary Faranell, the chief scientist of the Royal Apothecary Society, operating with the full authority and patronage of Queen Sylvanas Windrunner.",["al"]={"apothecarium leader","who runs the apothecarium","faranell undercity"},["q"]="Who leads the Apothecarium?"},{["a"]="Their primary endeavor is cultivating a lethal New Plague engineered to annihilate both the Scourge forces of the Lich King and any living human resistance contesting Forsaken territory in Lordaeron.",["al"]={"forsaken plague research","new plague undercity","what are they brewing"},["q"]="What is the Royal Apothecary Society trying to create?"},{["a"]="Yes. The district is the capital's main hub for alchemists and herbalists, hosting advanced profession trainers along its walkways and chambers.",["al"]={"apothecarium trainers","alchemy in undercity","undercity herbalism trainer"},["q"]="Can players learn professions here?"}},["kw"]={"abominations","alchemy","apothecarium","faranell","new plague","royal apothecary society","sylvanas","undercity"},["n"]="Apothecarium",["s"]="The Apothecarium is the southwestern quarter of the Undercity and the headquarters of the Royal Apothecary Society. Within these noxious laboratories, Forsaken alchemists labor tirelessly under Master Apothecary Faranell to concoct virulent plagues, toxins, and engineered horrors. It stands as the grim heart of Undercity's biological research, vital to Lady Sylvanas's campaign against the living and the Scourge.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Occupying the southwestern terrace of the subterranean capital, the Apothecarium is a labyrinth of bubbling vats, dissection tables, and pungent chemical fumes. Led by Master Apothecary Faranell, the Royal Apothecary Society utilizes this district to advance their understanding of mortality and rot. Here, alchemists and surgeons experiment on tissue grafts, vivisection, and the assembly of mighty abominations. Their overriding purpose, mandated by Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, is the formulation of a new plague capable of eradicating both the Scourge and the lingering human presence across Lordaeron.",["t"]="Chamber of Horrors"},{["b"]="Beyond grand military ambitions, the quarter serves as the premier center of practical alchemy and herbalism for the Horde in the Eastern Kingdoms. Initiates and masters alike gather beside toxic canals to distill concoctions, study botanical blights, and consult master practitioners.",["t"]="Center of Forsaken Alchemy"}}}}}
t["subzone:astranaar"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,315,19.477.0,21.497.0,41.223.0,47.190.0,68.231.0,41.133.0",["h"]="e9b671",["n"]="Astranaar",["s"]="Astranaar. Astranaar es el principal asentamiento de elfos de la noche en el centro de Vallefresno, construido a lo largo de una serena isla en un lago que se extiende a ambos lados del antiguo camino del bosque. Al actuar como el corazón palpitante de las operaciones de la Alianza en la región, proporciona un refugio vital a los viajeros que se enfrentan a las crecientes amenazas de los fúrbolgs hostiles, los sátiros y la Horda. Situada sobre una isla en medio de un lago forestal, Astranaar se erige como el mayor asentamiento de elfos de la noche de Vallefresno. Conectada a tierra firme por pasarelas de madera que cruzan las aguas, la localidad alberga centinelas, sacerdotisas y artesanos que vigilan los bosques. Además de ofrecer comodidades básicas como una posada, comerciantes y un peletero experto, sus perchas elevadas cuentan con un maestro de vuelo que ofrece viajes en hipogrifo a puestos remotos por todo Kalimdor.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Astranaar serves as the Alliance's command post and primary logistical hub while maneuvering through the contested wilderness of Ashenvale.",["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, Astranaar is the central bastion of their ancient homeland in central Kalimdor, safeguarding sacred groves and housing the grave of fallen hero Valstann Staghelm."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Astranaar offers a full suite of amenities for Alliance travelers, including an inn, general goods vendors, an expert leatherworking trainer, and a flight master connecting to key outposts throughout Ashenvale and Kalimdor.",["al"]={"astranaar amenities","what is in astranaar","astranaar flight master"},["q"]="What services are available in Astranaar?"},{["a"]="The cemetery by the lake contains the tomb of Valstann Staghelm, son of Archdruid Fandral Staghelm, who was slain during the ancient War of the Shifting Sands against the Qiraji in Silithus.",["al"]={"astranaar grave","valstann staghelm grave","who is buried here"},["q"]="Who is buried in the graveyard across the lake?"},{["a"]="The Thistlefur furbolgs to the north have fallen under dark, corrupting influences. Sentinel Raene Wolfrunner fears that left unchecked, their growing aggression will embolden them to mount an open assault against Astranaar itself.",["al"]={"thistlefur threat","why fight furbolgs","raene wolfrunner quest"},["q"]="Why are the Sentinels in Astranaar worried about the local furbolgs?"},{["a"]="No. Astranaar is a heavily fortified Alliance stronghold guarded by armed Night Elf Sentinels who will attack Horde members on sight.",["al"]={"is astranaar friendly to horde","horde in astranaar"},["q"]="Can Horde players visit Astranaar safely?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","astranaar","kalimdor","night elf","raene wolfrunner","sentinels","thistlefur","valstann staghelm"},["n"]="Astranaar",["s"]="Astranaar is the primary Night Elf settlement in central Ashenvale, built across a serene lake island straddling the ancient forest road. Serving as the beating heart of Alliance operations in the region, it provides vital refuge to travelers facing encroaching threats from hostile furbolgs, satyrs, and the Horde.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated atop an island in the middle of a forest lake, Astranaar stands as the largest night elven settlement in Ashenvale. Connected to the mainland by wooden footbridges spanning the waters, the town houses sentinels, priests, and artisans who keep vigil over the woodlands. In addition to offering basic comforts such as an inn, traders, and an expert leatherworker, its elevated perches host a flight master providing hippogryph travel to distant outposts across Kalimdor.",["t"]="Heart of the Forest"},{["b"]="Despite its tranquil waters and glowing lanterns, Astranaar exists in a state of perpetual readiness. Local leaders like Raene Wolfrunner coordinate patrols and defensive actions against the corrupted Thistlefur furbolgs encroaching from the north, fearful they may mount a direct assault on the settlement. The town also bears quiet historical sorrow: across the lake in the cemetery lies the resting place of Valstann Staghelm, who fell a thousand years ago during the War of the Shifting Sands.",["t"]="A Bastion Under Siege"}}}}}
t["subzone:auberdine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,353,28.711.0,19.550.0,35.261.0,20.188.0,60.308.0,57.277.0",["h"]="7bb0a2",["n"]="Auberdine",["s"]="Auberdine. Auberdine es una ciudad portuaria costera de elfos de la noche en las sombrías costas de Costa Oscura, que sirve como la principal puerta de entrada marítima de la Alianza al norte de Kalimdor. Cobijada bajo cielos encapotados y riscos cubiertos de pinos, conecta el hogar insular de Teldrassil con los Reinos del Este, a la vez que actúa como un refugio administrativo frente a la naturaleza circundante. Asentada a orillas del Mar de la Bruma, Auberdine es el único asentamiento importante que ha logrado perdurar en la Costa Oscura moderna. A diferencia de las aisladas ciudades en las copas de los árboles de Teldrassil, Auberdine mira hacia el exterior, sirviendo como el puerto más transitado de la Alianza en el norte. Barcos regulares navegan entre aquí y el Puerto de Menethil en los Reinos del Este, mientras que los transbordadores locales viajan a Aldea Rut'theran, a las ramas del Árbol del Mundo. Debido a su papel comercial, Auberdine acoge un ambiente más cosmopolita que los enclaves élficos tradicionales; los visitantes encuentran farolas que iluminan calles empedradas, carteles bilingües en darnassiano y común, y comerciantes de tierras lejanas, incluidos enanos y gnomos, mezclándose entre las casas bajas de madera arqueada.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="This port is the lifeblood of Alliance travel and supply lines into northern Kalimdor, ensuring steady logistics between Stormwind, Ironforge, and Darnassus.",["race:NightElf"]="For kaldorei venturing out from Teldrassil, Auberdine is the first true mainland hub where ancient tradition meets the strange ways and bustling industry of younger Alliance allies."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The docks connect northern Kalimdor to the wider Alliance world. One pier hosts the ferry to Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil, while another berths large ocean-going vessels that sail across the Great Sea directly to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",["al"]={"auberdine boats","where do boats go","auberdine travel"},["q"]="Where do the ships in Auberdine go?"},{["a"]="Auberdine is stewarded by elder Thundris Windweaver alongside the Auberdine Village Council. The settlement's defense is overseen by the Sentinels, led locally by Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea.",["al"]={"auberdine leader","who is in charge","village council"},["q"]="Who rules Auberdine?"},{["a"]="Because Auberdine serves as the Alliance's chief port on northern Kalimdor, foreign traders, craftsmen, and travelers arrive here first. Dwarves have set up a local smithy to service visiting ships and travellers, making the town unusually diverse and welcoming compared to traditional night elf settlements.",["al"]={"non elves in auberdine","why dwarves here"},["q"]="Why are there dwarves and humans living in a night elf town?"},{["a"]="Traditionalists and isolationists in Darnassus often regard Auberdine as tainted by worldly commerce and outland influences. Some orthodox elves consider its people to be misfits, and the bustling trade hub is viewed as poorly suited to strictly traditional druidic lifestyles.",["al"]={"darnassus auberdine rivalry","auberdine outcasts"},["q"]="Why do night elves from Darnassus look down on Auberdine?"}},["kw"]={"auberdine","boat","darkshore","docks","kaldorei","lighthouse","port","sentinels","thundris windweaver"},["n"]="Auberdine",["s"]="Auberdine is a coastal night elven port town on the gloomy shores of Darkshore, serving as the Alliance's primary maritime gateway to northern Kalimdor. Sheltered beneath overcast skies and pine-covered bluffs, it connects the island home of Teldrassil to the Eastern Kingdoms while serving as an administrative haven against the encroaching wilderness.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Resting along the shores of the Veiled Sea, Auberdine is the only major settlement to successfully endure in modern Darkshore. Unlike the secluded treetop cities of Teldrassil, Auberdine looks outward, serving as the Alliance's busiest port in the north. Regular ships sail between here and Menethil Harbor in the Eastern Kingdoms, while local ferries run to Rut'theran Village at the boughs of the World Tree. Because of its trade role, Auberdine embraces a more cosmopolitan air than traditional elven enclaves; visitors find lamps illuminating stone-laid streets, bilingual signs in Darnassian and Common, and outland merchants including dwarves and gnomes mingling among the low-slung, arched timber houses.",["t"]="Gateway to Northern Kalimdor"},{["b"]="Governed by elder Thundris Windweaver and the Auberdine Village Council, the town coordinates the defence of Darkshore alongside the local Sentinels. Despite its role as a vital trade hub, highborn denizens of Darnassus often look askance at Auberdine, viewing its population of traders, fishermen, and outsiders as misfits. The town endures relentless regional perils: aggressive murlocs raid the fishing boats along the strand, corrupted Blackwood furbolgs press from the south, and foul magic seeping down from Felwood agitates the local wildlife.",["t"]="A Beleaguered Haven"}}}}}
t["subzone:azurelode-mine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,261,22.430.0,23.300.0,28.163.0,39.197.0,44.199.0,27.63.0",["h"]="0908c1",["n"]="Mina Azur",["s"]="Mina Azur. Mina Azur es una activa mina de hierro de la Alianza situada en las colinas suroccidentales de Laderas de Trabalomas. Custodiada por la milicia de Costasur y trabajada por peones humanos, su constante suministro de mineral abastece el esfuerzo bélico humano local contra los Renegados de Molino Tarren. Situada al suroeste de las tierras de cultivo abiertas y justo al oeste de Costasur, Mina Azur lleva mucho tiempo extrayendo las riquezas minerales de las crestas a lo largo de la costa. Antes de que se sellara la Muralla de Cringrís, estas colinas se consideraban parte del territorio gilneano. Hoy en día, los mineros humanos trabajan a gran profundidad bajo la atenta mirada de Foreman Bonds, extrayendo hierro para forjar armas y armaduras destinadas a los defensores de la Alianza que defienden la región frente a Entrañas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Striking at Azurelode Mine cuts off Southshore's supply of fresh iron, directly supporting the Forsaken offensive in the Foothills.",["profession:Mining"]="The tunnels inside and the ridges around Azurelode are rich in iron deposits, though Alliance miners guard the interior fiercely."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Azurelode Mine is controlled by the Alliance and operated by human miners affiliated with Southshore and the Hillsbrad township, overseen on-site by Foreman Bonds.",["al"]={"who runs azurelode","azurelode mine faction","who owns azurelode"},["q"]="Who controls Azurelode Mine?"},{["a"]="The mine supplies vital iron to the armories of Southshore and local Alliance militia. Tarren Mill's leadership targets the miners and overseers to cripple human weapon production in the Foothills.",["al"]={"why attack azurelode","battle of hillsbrad mine","horde interest in mine"},["q"]="Why is the mine important to the Horde?"},{["a"]="Historically, the rugged ridge holding Azurelode Mine fell within the outer borders of Gilneas before King Genn Greymane erected the Greymane Wall, walling his kingdom off from the rest of Lordaeron.",["al"]={"greymane wall history","was azurelode gilneas","gilneas mine"},["q"]="Was Azurelode Mine always part of Hillsbrad?"},{["a"]="The mine primarily produces iron ore for nearby human armories.",["al"]={"what ore in azurelode","azurelode resources"},["q"]="What metals are mined here?"}},["kw"]={"azurelode mine","foreman bonds","hillsbrad foothills","hillsbrad miners","iron mine","southshore"},["n"]="Azurelode Mine",["s"]="Azurelode Mine is an active Alliance iron mine nestled in the southwestern hills of Hillsbrad Foothills. Guarded by Southshore's militia and worked by human laborers, its steady supply of ore fuels the local human war effort against the Forsaken of Tarren Mill.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated southwest of the open farmland and just west of Southshore, Azurelode Mine has long tapped into the mineral-rich ridges along the coast. Before the Greymane Wall was sealed, these hills were considered part of Gilnean territory. Today, human miners labor deep underground under the watchful eye of Foreman Bonds, extracting iron to forge arms and armor for the Alliance defenders holding the region against the Undercity.",["t"]="Veins of the Foothills"},{["b"]="Because Azurelode Mine supplies the bulk of the raw iron needed to maintain Southshore's garrisons and town militia, it sits directly in the crosshairs of the Horde. Tarren Mill has targeted its workforce and guards in an effort to shatter the supply lines that sustain Hillsbrad's human strongholds.",["t"]="A Vital Military Target"}}}}}
t["subzone:bael-dun-digsite"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,299,22.420.0,26.432.0,35.308.0,52.266.0,55.172.0,59.263.0",["h"]="98ac2f",["n"]="Excavación Bael'Dun",["s"]="Excavación Bael'Dun. La Excavación Bael'Dun es una excavación enana horadada en lo profundo de las montañas a lo largo del confín occidental de Mulgore. Establecida por el equipo del Prospector Khazgorm desde Bael Modan, la cantera es considerada por los tauren locales como una profanación directa de su tierra ancestral y un insulto a la Madre Tierra. Emplazada en las laderas montañosas del oeste de Mulgore, la Excavación Bael'Dun representa el punto más meridional de la expedición de la Liga de Expedicionarios enana con base en Bael Modan, en el sur de Los Baldíos. Sin preocuparse por las fronteras territoriales ni por las tradiciones espirituales de las tribus recién asentadas, los prospectores enanos llegaron con picos, palas y pólvora para desenterrar antiguas reliquias de los titanes enterradas bajo las llanuras.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Though driven by an earnest thirst for historical discovery, the Bael'dun miners have overextended deep into sovereign Horde territory, sparking violent friction with the locals.",["race:Tauren"]="The intrusive scarring of Mulgore's western hills makes Bael'dun a direct insult to the Earth Mother, demanding decisive action to protect ancestral soil from foreign desecration."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The prospectors belong to the dwarven expedition headquartered at Bael Modan in the southern Barrens. Driven by the Explorers' League's quest to uncover ancient artifacts and Titan heritage, they established this outpost wherever their instruments suggested relics might lie, disregarding tauren sovereignty.",["al"]={"why are dwarves here","dwarves in mulgore","baeldun dwarves"},["q"]="Why are dwarves digging in Mulgore?"},{["a"]="The tauren view the operation as an intolerable wound against the Earth Mother. After the dwarves refused early warnings to leave peacefully, Baine Bloodhoof and the village leaders sent warriors to destroy the miners' tools and drive the trespassers out of Mulgore.",["al"]={"what do tauren think","baine reaction","tauren response to digsite"},["q"]="How does the Bloodhoof tribe respond to the digsite?"},{["a"]="Bael'dun is a satellite digsite established directly from the fortress and primary excavation at Bael Modan, located just across the mountain ridge in the southern Barrens.",["al"]={"bael modan link","where do these dwarves come from"},["q"]="What is the connection between Bael'dun and Bael Modan?"},{["a"]="Baine Bloodhoof initially pursued diplomatic solutions and issued formal warnings to the expedition leaders. However, the dwarves treated Mulgore as unclaimed wilderness and completely ignored tauren spiritual concerns, leaving force as the tribe's only recourse.",["al"]={"did tauren try peace","diplomacy with dwarves"},["q"]="Why didn't the tauren simply negotiate with the expedition?"}},["kw"]={"bael modan","bael'dun","baeldun","baine bloodhoof","digsite","dwarves","earth mother","explorers league","mulgore"},["n"]="Bael'dun Digsite",["s"]="The Bael'dun Digsite is a dwarven excavation carved deep into the mountains along the western edge of Mulgore. Established by Prospector Khazgorm's team out of Bael Modan, the quarry is viewed by the local tauren as a direct desecration of their ancestral homeland and an insult to the Earth Mother.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched on the mountain slopes of western Mulgore, the Bael'dun Digsite represents the southernmost reach of the dwarven Explorers' League expedition based out of Bael Modan in the southern Barrens. Unconcerned with territorial borders or the spiritual traditions of the newly settled tribes, dwarven prospectors arrived with picks, shovels, and blasting powder to unearth ancient Titan relics buried beneath the plains.",["t"]="Intrusion in the Hills"},{["b"]="The Bloodhoof tribe viewed this invasive quarrying as an outright assault on the Earth Mother. Baine Bloodhoof initially urged caution and attempted to warn the interlopers away, but the dwarves flatly refused to abandon their trenches. Concluding that diplomacy had failed, the tauren resolved to break the expedition's tools and forcibly expel the miners before their destructive digging tears further into Mulgore's sacred earth.",["t"]="Defending the Earth Mother"}}}}}
t["subzone:bael-dun-keep"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,304,32.528.0,25.523.0,27.162.0,51.142.0,49.187.0,38.102.0",["h"]="e0ca68",["n"]="Fortaleza de Bael'dun",["s"]="Fortaleza de Bael'dun. La Fortaleza de Bael'dun es una imponente fortificación enana que domina la excavación de Bael Modan en el sur de Los Baldíos. Bajo el mando del General Twinbraid, esta fortaleza afianza la controvertida presencia de la Alianza en la región, lo que la enfrenta en un violento conflicto con los territorios circundantes de la Horda. Construida según los diseños del arquitecto enano Haggis Boatmurder, la Fortaleza de Bael'dun sirve como el corazón militar fortificado de la presencia de Forjaz en el sur de Los Baldíos. Elevándose sobre las extensas trincheras de excavación de Bael Modan, la fortaleza protege a los prospectores y arqueólogos que buscan antiguos artefactos de los titanes. Fuertemente armada con herrería y artillería, su guarnición mantiene una vigilancia constante, asegurando las líneas de suministro enanas y proyectando el poder marcial de la Alianza directamente en el corazón de Kalimdor.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="This keep is your primary military toehold in the southern Barrens, guarding the vital discoveries of the Explorers' League against hostile Horde forces.",["race:Tauren"]="Bael'dun Keep stands on sacred grounds stolen from the Stonespire tribe, serving as an insulting reminder of Alliance encroachment on your homeland."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The fortress is garrisoned by dwarven soldiers answering to the Alliance and the Explorers' League of Ironforge, led by the steadfast commander General Twinbraid.",["al"]={"who runs bael'dun keep","who leads baeldun","general twinbraid"},["q"]="Who controls Bael'dun Keep?"},{["a"]="It was established to defend Bael Modan, a massive archaeological expedition digging for titan relics and ancient dwarven origins in Kalimdor.",["al"]={"why are dwarves in the barrens","purpose of bael'dun keep","why did dwarves build here"},["q"]="Why is Bael'dun Keep built in the southern Barrens?"},{["a"]="The excavation and fortress displaced the native Stonespire tauren from their ancestral grounds. Survivors like Gann Stonespire seek vengeance and the destruction of the dwarven invaders.",["al"]={"gann stonespire revenge","why do tauren hate baeldun","stonespire feud"},["q"]="Why are the local tauren attacking Bael'dun Keep?"},{["a"]="Dwarven architectural records indicate the fortress was designed and constructed by Haggis Boatmurder.",["al"]={"who built bael'dun keep","haggis boatmurder","baeldun schematics"},["q"]="Who was the architect of the fortress?"}},["kw"]={"bael modan","bael'dun keep","baeldun","explorers' league","gann stonespire","general twinbraid","haggis boatmurder","southern barrens"},["n"]="Bael'dun Keep",["s"]="Bael'dun Keep is an imposing dwarven fortification overlooking the Bael Modan excavation in the southern Barrens. Under the command of General Twinbraid, this fortress anchors the Alliance's controversial presence in the region, bringing them into violent conflict with the surrounding Horde territories.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Constructed according to designs by the dwarven architect Haggis Boatmurder, Bael'dun Keep serves as the fortified military heart of the Ironforge presence in the southern Barrens. Towering over the expansive excavation trenches of Bael Modan, the fortress protects the Prospectors and archaeologists searching for ancient titan artifacts. Heavily armed with ironworks and artillery, its garrison maintains a vigilant watch, securing dwarven supply lines and projecting Alliance martial power straight into Kalimdor's heartland.",["t"]="A Dwarven Stronghold in Kalimdor"},{["b"]="The construction of Bael'dun Keep and the adjoining digsite did not come peacefully; it displaced the local Stonespire tribe of tauren from their ancestral home. Now, Bael'dun sits as a simmering flashpoint in the Barrens. Nearby Horde outposts view the fortress as a flagrant military intrusion, while Gann Stonespire wages a personal war of vengeance against the invaders. Between aggrieved tauren, opportunistic scouts, and suspicious outposts like Camp Taurajo, the keep is constantly under threat of raid and sabotage.",["t"]="A Flashpoint of Bloodshed"}}}}}
t["subzone:bael-modan"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,281,31.560.0,29.490.1,39.246.0,50.245.0,23.302.0,30.181.1",["h"]="b0b4b9",["n"]="Bael Modan",["s"]="Bael Modan. Bael Modan es un puesto de avanzada enano fortificado y una excavación arqueológica situada en el sur de Los Baldíos. Establecida por excavadores enanos que buscan antiguas reliquias de los titanes, esta instalación fuertemente armada ha desatado un amargo conflicto al desplazar a los tauren Picopiedra indígenas. Bael Modan se compone de la fortificada Fortaleza de Bael'dun, un despliegue de enormes cañones de asedio, pistas de aterrizaje para girocópteros y una profunda fosa de excavación a cielo abierto. Los prospectores enanos llegaron a Kalimdor convencidos de que una antigua instalación de los titanes yace sepultada bajo la tierra roja. Sin embargo, sus voladuras atravesaron directamente tierras sagradas pertenecientes a los tauren Picopiedra. En lugar de negociar, la expedición enana expulsó a los Picopiedra de sus tierras ancestrales a base de disparos y explosivos, dejando a los miembros supervivientes de la tribu dispersos y sedientos de venganza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,1},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Dwarf"]="The dig site represents the Explorers' League's relentless drive to uncover Titan history, though its commanders' heavy-handed tactics have earned the fierce enmity of the local tribes.",["race:Tauren"]="Bael Modan stands as an open wound in the Barrens, built atop the ruins of the Stonespire tribe's sacred grounds. Helping Gann Stonespire extract vengeance is a matter of tribal honor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The dwarves are searching for ancient Titan structures and relics buried beneath Kalimdor. Their excavations are part of a broader expedition to uncover the origins of their race, which they believe are linked to buried Titan research facilities.",["al"]={"why are dwarves here","bael modan purpose","what are dwarves digging for"},["q"]="Why are dwarves digging in the Barrens?"},{["a"]="The land originally belonged to the Stonespire tribe, who considered the hills holy ground. When the dwarves arrived, they used explosives to blast open the dig site, slaughtering or driving away the resident tauren and destroying their village.",["al"]={"stonespire tauren","who lived at bael modan","tauren village"},["q"]="What happened to the tauren who used to live here?"},{["a"]="Gann Stonespire is one of the few surviving members of the Stonespire tribe. After attempts at a peaceful resolution failed, he camps near the road outside Bael Modan and enlists Horde travelers to sabotage the dwarven flying machines and kill the officers responsible for destroying his people's home.",["al"]={"gann","gann questgiver"},["q"]="Who is Gann Stonespire?"},{["a"]="The Tear of the Moons is a mysterious artifact unearthed by the excavators. It drives mortals who handle it mad, and it has left the exiled dwarf Feegly obsessed with reclaiming it.",["al"]={"tear of the moons relic","feegly artifact"},["q"]="What is the Tear of the Moons?"}},["kw"]={"bael modan","bael'dun","barrens excavation","feegly","gann stonespire","stonespire","tear of the moons","twinbraid"},["n"]="Bael Modan",["s"]="Bael Modan is a fortified dwarven outpost and archaeological dig site located in the southern Barrens. Established by dwarven excavators searching for ancient Titan relics, the heavily armed installation has ignited a bitter conflict by displacing the indigenous Stonespire tauren.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Bael Modan consists of the fortified Bael'dun Keep, an array of massive siege cannons, gyrocopter landing pads, and a deep open excavation pit. Dwarven prospectors arrived in Kalimdor under the conviction that an ancient Titan facility rests buried beneath the red earth. However, their blasting operations ripped directly through sacred ground belonging to the Stonespire tauren. Rather than negotiating, the dwarven expedition drove the Stonespire off their ancestral lands with gunfire and explosives, leaving the surviving tribesmen scattered and vengeful.",["t"]="Unearthed Secrets and Bloodshed"},{["b"]="The excavation has unearthed far more than historical stonework. Dwarven diggers recently uncovered an artifact known as the Tear of the Moons, a relic that induced paranoia and madness in those near it. One banished prospector, Feegly the Exiled, succumbed entirely to its influence, only to be twisted into a trogg the moment the stone returned to his grasp. Between deadly relics and the enraged tauren seeking retribution outside the gates, the dwarven camp stands under constant peril.",["t"]="The Price of Unearthed Relics"}}}}}
t["subzone:balnir-farmstead"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,385,24.502.0,35.561.0,57.306.0,45.263.0,45.283.0,46.212.0",["h"]="f6e3c4",["n"]="Hacienda Balnir",["s"]="Hacienda Balnir. La Hacienda Balnir es una finca abandonada en el este de Claros de Tirisfal, al noreste de las Ruinas de Lordaeron. Antaño célebre por criar a los afamados caballos blancos predilectos de la familia real de Lordaeron, estas tierras yacen ahora arruinadas e infestadas de miembros errantes de la Plaga. En la actualidad, la hacienda se alza como un sombrío monumento a los primeros años de vida del príncipe Arthas Menethil y el lugar donde reclamó a su corcel no-muerto. Durante generaciones, la familia Balnir crio a los legendarios sementales blancos de Lordaeron desde su propiedad en las onduladas colinas de Tirisfal. Siendo un niño, el príncipe Arthas Menethil visitaba a menudo la granja para escapar de la vida en la corte real, entablando amistad con el joven Jarim Balnir. Fue aquí donde Arthas presenció y ayudó en el parto del potro al que bautizó como Invencible. Años más tarde, después de que un trágico accidente de equitación acabara con la vida del corcel, Invencible recibió sepultura en las tierras de la hacienda a petición personal de Arthas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Forsaken magi are dispatched to these blighted grounds to gather surviving Balnir snapdragons, studying them to detect the lingering magical taint of the Scourge.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the farmstead is a bitter reminder of the prince who doomed Lordaeron, as well as a nagging security breach where Scourge from the Plaguelands slip behind the Bulwark."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Arthas spent much of his youth sneaking away to the farmstead to play with the breeder's son. He was present for the birth of his beloved horse, Invincible, and later buried the beast here after a fatal fall. Following his descent into darkness, Arthas returned to exhume and raise Invincible into undeath.",["al"]={"arthas farm","invincible birthplace","balnir arthas connection"},["q"]="Why is the Balnir Farmstead significant to Prince Arthas?"},{["a"]="The farm was managed by Jorum Balnir, his wife Vara, and their son Jarim. They were master horse breeders who raised prized white horses for Lordaeron's nobility. The entire family was slaughtered when Arthas's Scourge swept through Tirisfal during the Third War.",["al"]={"who owned balnir farm","balnir family","jorum balnir"},["q"]="Who lived at the farmstead before the plague?"},{["a"]="Mindless Scourge often slip past the Bulwark from the Plaguelands and gather at the farmstead, threatening the eastern approaches to Tirisfal. Additionally, Undercity scholars study the resilient snapdragons still growing in the gardens to measure the spread of plague contamination.",["al"]={"why forsaken care about balnir","rear guard patrol lore","balnir snapdragons"},["q"]="Why are the Forsaken monitoring the farm now?"},{["a"]="After Invincible died in a riding accident, Arthas asked that his beloved horse be buried on the farmstead's grounds. After returning as a death knight during the Third War, Arthas raised Invincible into undeath.",["al"]={"invincible burial","invincible grave","arthas horse burial"},["q"]="Why was Invincible buried at Balnir Farmstead?"}},["kw"]={"arthas","balnir","farmstead","horses","invincible","jorum","snapdragon","tirisfal"},["n"]="Balnir Farmstead",["s"]="The Balnir Farmstead is a derelict estate in eastern Tirisfal Glades, northeast of the Ruins of Lordaeron. Once renowned for raising the famed white horses favored by Lordaeron's royal family, the lands now lie ruined and infested by wandering Scourge. Today, the estate stands as a somber monument to Prince Arthas Menethil's early life and the site where he claimed his undead steed.",["sec"]={{["b"]="For generations, the Balnir family bred the legendary white stallions of Lordaeron from their homestead in the rolling hills of Tirisfal. As a boy, Prince Arthas Menethil frequently visited the farm to escape royal court life, befriending the young Jarim Balnir. It was here that Arthas assisted in the foaling of the colt he named Invincible. Years later, after a tragic riding accident claimed the steed's life, Invincible was laid to rest in the soil of the farmstead upon Arthas's personal request.",["t"]="A Legacy of Royal Steeds"},{["b"]="When Prince Arthas returned from Northrend and sacked Capital City, the Scourge wiped out the Balnir family without mercy. Newly fallen as a death knight, Arthas marched to the farmstead to exhume and resurrect Invincible with Frostmourne, leaving behind an open, ransacked grave. In the wake of the Third War, the ruins serve as a foothold for mindless Scourge slipping past the Bulwark. Forsaken deathguards watch the farm warily, while Undercity magi harvest surviving snapdragons from the garden to test how deeply plague corruption has crept into the soil.",["t"]="Desolation and Scourge Infiltration"}}}}}
t["subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,368,19.540.0,23.472.0,29.189.0,51.224.0,40.159.0,43.209.0",["h"]="9b5ed7",["n"]="Túmulo de Ben'ethil",["s"]="Túmulo de Ben'ethil. El Túmulo de Ben'ethil es un santuario subterráneo sagrado excavado en el interior de las raíces de Teldrassil. Creado originalmente como lugar de descanso para los durmientes Druidas de la Garfa, el complejo de cavernas ha caído recientemente en el caos. Los fúrbolgs corruptos de la tribu Tuercepinos han invadido sus cámaras, convirtiendo un lugar de pacífico letargo en una peligrosa guarida de locura. Los túmulos sirven como sagradas cámaras de descanso donde los druidas elfos de la noche duermen mientras proyectan sus espíritus hacia el Sueño Esmeralda. El Túmulo de Ben'ethil estaba dedicado específicamente a cobijar a los Druidas de la Garfa mientras comulgaban con la naturaleza. Dividido en cámaras subterráneas superiores e inferiores, el cubil antaño resonaba con una tranquila ensoñación y una profunda magia meditativa. Sin embargo, la aflicción que asola a la fauna de Teldrassil no perdonó a los fúrbolgs Tuercepinos, quienes invadieron el complejo y convirtieron sus salas excavadas en una madriguera fortificada.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Ban'ethil represents sacred ground for the Cenarion Circle, specifically built to protect Druids of the Talon while communing with the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="The occupation of Ban'ethil by corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs is an alarming sign of the growing sickness plaguing their new home of Teldrassil."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Ban'ethil Barrow Den is a subterranean hollow in Teldrassil crafted by the night elves. It was designed to shelter sleeping Druids of the Talon while their spirits roamed the Emerald Dream.",["al"]={"what is ban'ethil","ban'ethil barrow den purpose","what is this cave"},["q"]="What is Ban'ethil Barrow Den?"},{["a"]="The Gnarlpine furbolgs have fallen victim to a spreading corruption affecting Teldrassil's creatures. Driven hostile and territorial, they invaded the barrow den, displacing the keepers and threatening the slumbering druids.",["al"]={"why are gnarlpine in ban'ethil","furbolgs in barrow den","who took over ban'ethil"},["q"]="Why are there furbolgs inside Ban'ethil Barrow Den?"},{["a"]="The cavern complex is split into two primary interconnected tiers: the Upper Den near the entrance passages and the Lower Den deeper in the subterranean roots.",["al"]={"ban'ethil layout","upper den lower den","ban'ethil levels"},["q"]="What are the sections of the barrow den?"},{["a"]="Barrow dens provide safe, secure physical shelter for druids who enter prolonged, deep slumbers to project their consciousness into the Emerald Dream, leaving their waking bodies helpless for years or decades.",["al"]={"why do druids sleep in barrows","druid barrow dens lore","emerald dream barrow den"},["q"]="Why are barrow dens so important to druids?"}},["kw"]={"ban'ethil","barrow den","druids of the talon","emerald dream","furbolg","gnarlpine","teldrassil"},["n"]="Ban'ethil Barrow Den",["s"]="Ban'ethil Barrow Den is a sacred subterranean sanctuary hollowed out within the roots of Teldrassil. Originally created as a resting place for the sleeping Druids of the Talon, the cavern complex has recently fallen into chaos. The corrupted furbolgs of the Gnarlpine tribe have overrun its chambers, turning a place of peaceful slumber into a perilous den of madness.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Barrow dens serve as sacred resting chambers where night elf druids slumber while projecting their spirits into the Emerald Dream. Ban'ethil Barrow Den was dedicated specifically to sheltering the Druids of the Talon as they communed with nature. Divided into upper and lower subterranean chambers, the den once resonated with tranquil reverie and deep meditative magic. However, the affliction sweeping Teldrassil's wildlife did not spare the Gnarlpine furbolgs, who invaded the complex, turning its hollowed halls into a fortified warren.",["t"]="A Defiled Sanctuary"},{["b"]="Driven mad by mysterious corruption taking root across the World Tree, the Gnarlpine tribe drove out or endangered the slumbering druids within Ban'ethil. The furbolgs now fiercely guard the winding tunnels, aggressive toward any night elf who approaches. For the defenders of Teldrassil, reclaiming the barrow den is an urgent priority, not merely to drive back the hostile furbolgs, but to protect the vulnerable druids and sacred relics trapped within its lower depths.",["t"]="The Gnarlpine Incursion"}}}}}
t["subzone:ban-ethil-hollow"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,317,17.529.0,34.165.0,34.262.0,66.236.0,44.239.0",["h"]="b34d6a",["n"]="Hondonada Ban'ethil",["s"]="Hondonada Ban'ethil. La Hondonada Ban'ethil es un barranco escarpado que se adentra en el bosque justo al sur del camino principal que conecta Dolanaar y Darnassus. Se ha convertido en un peligroso refugio para fúrbolgs corruptos y agresivos que representan una amenaza constante para los viajeros. Escondida en el fondo del barranco se encuentra la entrada al Túmulo de Ben'ethil. Situada junto al camino entre Dolanaar y Darnassus, la Hondonada Ban'ethil es un crudo recordatorio de que las ramas de Teldrassil no son del todo seguras. Los fúrbolgs enloquecidos por la extraña aflicción que asola el Árbol del Mundo se han refugiado por todo el descenso rocoso. Con frecuencia acechan el sendero cercano, esperando para emboscar a mensajeros incautos y centinelas errantes. En lo profundo del barranco se halla el umbral del Túmulo de Ben'ethil, donde druidas dormidos y túneles ancestrales se enfrentan a la invasión de las bestias enloquecidas del exterior.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The hollow conceals the entrance to Ban'ethil Barrow Den, sacred ground where druids traditionally rest to commune with the Emerald Dream, now endangered by rabid wildlife.",["race:NightElf"]="Seeing the furbolgs fall to madness so close to the road between Dolanaar and Darnassus is a grim sign of Teldrassil's mounting sickness, requiring young sentinels and druids to step in."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Ban'ethil Hollow is a ravine in central Teldrassil, located just south of the primary road running between the village of Dolanaar and the capital city of Darnassus.",["al"]={"banethil hollow location","where is ban'ethil hollow","find banethil hollow"},["q"]="Where is Ban'ethil Hollow located?"},{["a"]="The furbolgs across Teldrassil have succumbed to a spreading corruption and madness that grips the World Tree's wildlife. Instead of living peacefully alongside the night elves as they historically have, these tribes have become fiercely territorial and violent.",["al"]={"why are furbolgs mad","hostile furbolgs banethil","banethil furbolg attack"},["q"]="Why are the furbolgs here hostile?"},{["a"]="The Ban'ethil Barrow Den is an underground complex historically used by night elven druids to enter deep hibernation and commune with the Emerald Dream. However, with corruption rising in the hollow, the den has become dangerous ground.",["al"]={"what is in the barrow den","banethil barrow den","den in banethil hollow"},["q"]="What is inside the Ban'ethil Barrow Den at the back of the hollow?"},{["a"]="The main road is generally patrolled by night elf sentinels, but furbolgs from Ban'ethil Hollow often venture up from the ravine to ambush travelers. Travelers making the journey between Dolanaar and Darnassus should remain on their guard.",["al"]={"is the road safe","furbolg ambushes","road to darnassus safe"},["q"]="Is the road above the hollow safe to travel?"}},["kw"]={"ambush","ban'ethil barrow den","ban'ethil hollow","darnassus","dolanaar","furbolg","ravine","teldrassil"},["n"]="Ban'ethil Hollow",["s"]="Ban'ethil Hollow is a rugged ravine cutting into the woodland just south of the main road connecting Dolanaar and Darnassus. It has become a dangerous haven for corrupted, aggressive furbolgs who pose a constant threat to travelers. Tucked away in the back of the ravine lies the entrance to the Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated off the highway between Dolanaar and Darnassus, Ban'ethil Hollow is a sharp reminder that the boughs of Teldrassil are not entirely safe. Furbolgs driven mad by the strange affliction plaguing the World Tree have taken refuge throughout the rocky descent. They frequently stalk the nearby path, waiting to ambush unwary couriers and wandering sentinels. Deep within the ravine sits the threshold of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, where slumbering druids and ancient tunnels face encroachment from the maddened beasts outside.",["t"]="A Perilous Ravine"}}}}}
t["subzone:baradin-bay"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,315,20.484.0,23.504.0,47.178.0,55.190.0,55.183.0,37.172.0",["h"]="bb1060",["n"]="Bahía de Baradin",["s"]="Bahía de Baradin. La Bahía de Baradin es la extensa masa de agua situada entre las costas de Khaz Modan, los Humedales, las Tierras Altas de Arathi y el sur de Lordaeron. Antaño patrullada intensamente por la poderosa armada de Kul Tiras durante la Segunda Guerra, sus aguas ocultan ahora arrecifes traicioneros, buques de guerra hundidos y depredadores acuáticos hostiles. Enmarcada por las costas de Dun Morogh al sur y Lordaeron al norte, la Bahía de Baradin sirve como un paso marítimo vital que conecta los puertos de los Reinos del Este. La bahía cuenta con puertos de gran actividad como Puerto de Menethil en los Humedales y Costasur en las Laderas de Trabalomas. Sin embargo, navegar por estas aguas es peligroso: los bancos de arena poco profundos, los escollos escarpados y una fauna peligrosa compuesta por múrlocs, crocoliscos y tiburones de aguas profundas suponen una amenaza constante tanto para marineros como para viajeros.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Baradin Bay serves as the maritime lifeline connecting Alliance operations in Khaz Modan with their outposts in Arathi and Hillsbrad, though naval hazards and sunken wreckage make every crossing risky.",["race:Human"]="For humans, especially those tracing lineage back to Kul Tiras or Lordaeron, the bay is hallowed and somber ground holding the watery graves of Second War sailors."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The most prominent settlements on the bay's coast are Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands and Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills, which sustain vital naval transit across the sea.",["al"]={"baradin bay ports","harbors in baradin bay","where does baradin bay lead"},["q"]="What major ports are located along Baradin Bay?"},{["a"]="Many of the wrecks, including the Lost Fleet along the Wetlands shore and those resting on Drowned Reef, were ships of the Kul Tiras navy sunk during intense naval clashes in the Second War.",["al"]={"wetlands shipwrecks","why are ships sunken here","lost fleet origin"},["q"]="Why are there so many shipwrecks along the bay's coast?"},{["a"]="The shallows are crawling with aggressive murlocs and swamp crocolisks, while the deeper waters are infested with predatory crabs, sharks, and the restless spirits of drowned sailors.",["al"]={"baradin bay monsters","murlocs in baradin bay","is it safe to swim in baradin bay"},["q"]="What threats can be found in the waters of Baradin Bay?"},{["a"]="Baradin Bay is enclosed by northwestern Dun Morogh, the marshy shores of the Wetlands, the cliffs of the Arathi Highlands, and the coasts of southern Hillsbrad and Gilneas.",["al"]={"what zones border baradin bay","baradin bay geography"},["q"]="Which territories border Baradin Bay?"}},["kw"]={"baradin bay","drowned reef","great sea","kul tiras","lost fleet","menethil harbor","southshore","wetlands"},["n"]="Baradin Bay",["s"]="Baradin Bay is the expansive body of water lying between the shores of Khaz Modan, the Wetlands, the Arathi Highlands, and southern Lordaeron. Once vigorously patrolled by the powerful navy of Kul Tiras during the Second War, its waters now conceal treacherous reefs, sunken warships, and hostile aquatic predators.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Framed by the coasts of Dun Morogh to the south and Lordaeron to the north, Baradin Bay serves as a vital maritime passage connecting the harbors of the Eastern Kingdoms. The bay is anchored by busy ports like Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands and Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. However, navigating these waters is perilous: shallow sandbanks, jagged shoals, and dangerous fauna like murlocs, crocolisks, and deep-sea sharks pose constant threats to sailors and travelers alike.",["t"]="A Strategic Waterway"},{["b"]="During the Second War, Baradin Bay witnessed heavy naval conflict as the fleets of Kul Tiras clashed with the Horde. Today, grim reminders of those battles litter the coast and the seabed. The shattered hulls of the Kul Tiran Third Fleet—known locally as the Lost Fleet—rest half-submerged along the Wetlands coast, while other vessels have plummeted down to Drowned Reef. Hostile spirits, opportunistic salvagers, and ravenous sea beasts now haunt the waters surrounding these decaying timber ruins.",["t"]="Graveyard of the Fleets"}}}}}
t["subzone:bathran-s-haunt"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,277,38.528.0,29.506.0,33.144.0,26.202.0,23.154.0,41.171.0",["h"]="cd40b4",["n"]="Ruinas de Bathran",["s"]="Ruinas de Bathran. Ruinas de Bathran es una antigua ruina kaldorei ubicada en el noroeste de Vallefresno, al este de La Ensenada de Zoram. Recientemente, herboristas Renegados y sus guardianes se han apoderado del lugar para recolectar la flora local para sus investigaciones alquímicas, marchitando progresivamente el bosque circundante. Al norte de Las Ruinas de Ordil'Aran, pilares derruidos de elfos de la noche se yerguen engullidos por el espeso follaje de Vallefresno. Lo que otrora fue una tranquila reliquia kaldorei ha caído bajo la sombra de los Renegados. Merodeando entre el mármol roto, herboristas no-muertos y sus ejecutores han establecido un rudimentario laboratorio al aire libre. Su sola presencia corrompe el suelo ancestral: la hierba se pudre adoptando un tono pardo enfermizo, las flores vibrantes se marchitan y una descomposición antinatural avanza por la arboleda mientras recolectan metódicamente reactivos raros del bosque para sus experimentos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Herbalism"]="The ruins are botanically unique as the only known habitat for Bathran's Hair, an herb sought after for its rare remedial properties.",["race:NightElf"]="The Forsaken encampment at Bathran's Haunt is an outrage to kaldorei heritage, where undead intruders defile ancient elven stonework and blight the sacred soil."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Bathran's Haunt sits in northwestern Ashenvale, positioned directly north of the Ruins of Ordil'Aran and inland to the east of the Zoram Strand.",["al"]={"where is bathrans haunt","bathrans haunt location","how to get to bathrans haunt"},["q"]="Where is Bathran's Haunt located?"},{["a"]="Forsaken herbalists have established an encampment and laboratory among the ruins to gather and study the unique botanical life of the forest, most notably a rare remedial plant known as Bathran's Hair.",["al"]={"what are undead doing in ashenvale","why are forsaken at bathrans haunt","forsaken purpose bathran"},["q"]="Why are the Forsaken here?"},{["a"]="Bathran's Hair is a distinctive, valuable herb with potent restorative qualities that grows exclusively around the crumbling stonework of Bathran's Haunt.",["al"]={"bathrans hair plant","what is bathrans hair","bathran herb"},["q"]="What is Bathran's Hair?"},{["a"]="The prolonged presence and alchemical activities of the Forsaken have corrupted the immediate area, causing the grass to wither brown and delicate woodland flowers to die.",["al"]={"why is grass brown here","blight in bathrans haunt","why is the land decaying"},["q"]="Why is the ground dying around the ruins?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","bathran's hair","bathran's haunt","forsaken","herbalism","kaldorei ruins","ruins of ordil'aran","zoram strand"},["n"]="Bathran's Haunt",["s"]="Bathran's Haunt is an ancient kaldorei ruin nestled in northwestern Ashenvale, east of the Zoram Strand. Recently, Forsaken herbalists and their guardians have overtaken the site to harvest local flora for their alchemical research, steadily withering the surrounding woodland.",["sec"]={{["b"]="North of the Ruins of Ordil'Aran, crumbling night elf pillars stand swallowed by thick Ashenvale foliage. What was once a tranquil kaldorei relic has fallen under the shadow of the Forsaken. Skulking among the broken marble, undead herbalists and their enforcers have set up a crude open-air laboratory. Their presence alone blights the ancient soil: grass rots into a sickly brown, vibrant blossoms wilt, and an unnatural decay creeps through the grove as they methodically harvest rare woodland reagents for their experiments.",["t"]="A Blighted Refuge in the Ancient Woods"},{["b"]="The primary draw of these ruins is Bathran's Hair, a unique remedial herb found taking root only among these particular stones. While night elf and Alliance scouts view the Forsaken presence as a vile desecration of sacred elven soil, the undead work diligently to extract the plant's potent properties. The Horde maintains a vested interest in the compound's botanical yield, though the Forsaken's secretive methods and the resulting corruption of the earth draw suspicion from outsiders and allies alike.",["t"]="The Harvest of Bathran's Hair"}}}}}
t["subzone:beggar-s-haunt"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,297,27.594.0,38.408.0,41.251.0,48.233.0,43.202.0,48.155.0",["h"]="4d4d13",["n"]="Refugio de los Mendigos",["s"]="Refugio de los Mendigos. El Refugio de los Mendigos es una torre de vigilancia de Ventormenta abandonada, encaramada en una ladera del noreste del Bosque del Ocaso, cerca del camino de montaña hacia el Paso de la Muerte. Aunque en un principio se construyó para vigilar las fronteras orientales del reino, se ha convertido en un puesto de avanzada para infiltrados Renegados en pleno territorio de la Alianza. Encaramado sobre las brumosas colinas al este de la Mansión Mantoniebla, el Refugio de los Mendigos fue antaño un puesto de observación activo custodiado por la Guardia de Ventormenta para proteger los accesos orientales al reino. A medida que Grand Hamlet sucumbía a la penumbra del actual Bosque del Ocaso y las patrullas del reino se replegaban a Villa Oscura, la torre de piedra quedó abandonada a merced de los elementos. Hoy en día, su posición estratégica y dominante sirve a un propósito mucho más siniestro: agentes de los Renegados, entre ellos miembros de la Sociedad Real de Boticarios y Mortacechadores, utilizan la fortaleza en ruinas para investigar y vigilar la región en las mismas narices de la Alianza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The presence of Forsaken agents stationed inside an old Stormwind scout tower just off the main road is an alarming sign of Horde infiltration right on Darkshire's doorstep.",["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken operatives, this secluded outpost offers a rare and dangerous foothold deep within the human lands of the south."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Agents from the Undercity, including Apothecary Faustin of the Royal Apothecary Society and Deathstalker Zraedus, have claimed the abandoned watchtower. From here, they can monitor Alliance movements and quietly carry out experiments far to the south.",["al"]={"who is at beggars haunt","why is horde here","undead at beggars haunt"},["q"]="Why are there Forsaken at Beggar's Haunt?"},{["a"]="No. The tower was constructed as a scout outpost by the kingdom of Stormwind. When local defenses faltered and the region deteriorated into Duskwood, the Stormwind Guard abandoned it, leaving it empty until Forsaken scouts seized it.",["al"]={"who built beggars haunt","beggars haunt history","is this an alliance tower"},["q"]="Was this tower originally built by the Forsaken?"},{["a"]="Down the path behind the haunt lies Knight's Hollow, a secluded waterfall pool featuring an unmarked grave framed by hooded guardian statues identical in style to the monuments flanking the Dark Portal.",["al"]={"knights hollow statues","grave behind tower","dark portal statues duskwood"},["q"]="What is the strange grave behind the tower?"},{["a"]="Yes. The Forsaken stationed at the tower are seasoned agents who will strike down any Alliance adventurers that wander too close to their hillside redoubt.",["al"]={"will they attack me","beggars haunt guards","is beggars haunt safe"},["q"]="Is Beggar's Haunt hostile to Alliance travelers?"}},["kw"]={"apothecary faustin","beggar's haunt","deathstalker zraedus","duskwood","knight's hollow","scout tower","stormwind guard"},["n"]="Beggar's Haunt",["s"]="Beggar's Haunt is an abandoned Stormwind scout tower perched on a hillside in northeastern Duskwood, near the mountain road to Deadwind Pass. While originally built to keep watch over the kingdom's eastern borders, it has become an outpost for Forsaken infiltrators deep within Alliance territory.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched above the foggy hills east of Manor Mistmantle, Beggar's Haunt was once an active observation post manned by the Stormwind Guard to secure the eastern approaches to the realm. As Grand Hamlet collapsed into the gloom of modern Duskwood and kingdom patrols withdrew to Darkshire, the stone tower was abandoned to the elements. Today, its commanding vantage point serves a far more sinister purpose: agents of the Forsaken, including members of the Royal Apothecary Society and Deathstalkers, use the ruined stronghold to conduct research and monitor the region under the Alliance's nose.",["t"]="A Watchtower in the Shadows"},{["b"]="Behind the tower, a steep, twisting path descends to a secluded pool and waterfall known as Knight's Hollow. Here lies an unmarked grave flanked by two ominous hooded stone statues resembling the guardians flanking the Dark Portal. Nearby resting plots, including the burial site of an Unknown Soldier, speak to forgotten clashes fought along this frontier long before the Forsaken moved into the watchtower.",["t"]="Knight's Hollow and the Forgotten Dead"}}}}}
t["subzone:beren-s-peril"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,256,28.691.0,22.161.0,27.134.0,45.222.0,23.218.0",["h"]="0ecefe",["n"]="El Desafío de Beren",["s"]="El Desafío de Beren. El Desafío de Beren es una apartada caverna montañosa oculta en las colinas rocosas al suroeste de Molino Ámbar, en el Bosque de Argénteos. Sirve como reducto atrincherado para leales renegados de la Plaga que sirven al nigromante Thule Corvozarpa, conspirando contra los Renegados cercanos. Oculto en lo alto de los riscos al suroeste de Molino Ámbar, El Desafío de Beren consta de una sombría cueva y un serpenteante sendero de montaña escondidos de la calzada principal. Tras la devastación de la Tercera Guerra, no-muertos renegados de la Plaga bajo el mando del nigromante rebelde Thule Corvozarpa fortificaron este enclave. En lugar de someterse a la Dama Oscura o retirarse al norte, los siervos de Corvozarpa —regentes, guardianes y braceros— se reunieron aquí en secreto para preparar un asalto contra la base de los Renegados en El Sepulcro. Su presencia fue descubierta por exploradores renegados, convirtiendo el tranquilo acantilado en una zona de guerra activa para los operativos de la Horda enviados a eliminar la amenaza antes de que pudiera materializarse un ataque.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Securing the rugged paths of Silverpine Forest means clearing out rogue undead nests before they can sever supply lines between the Sepulcher and the southern territories.",["race:Undead"]="The Ravenclaw minions at Beren's Peril are a bitter reminder of the Scourge's lasting grip, threatening the safety of the Sepulcher and requiring swift, merciless eradication by Sylvanas's loyalists."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is a cave and surrounding hillside pass located southwest of Ambermill in Silverpine Forest, situated between the central highway and the Ambermill side road.",["al"]={"berens peril","where is berens peril","beren's peril cave"},["q"]="What is Beren's Peril?"},{["a"]="The cave is occupied by Scourge undead loyal to the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, including Ravenclaw guardians, drudgers, and regents.",["al"]={"who lives at berens peril","enemies at berens peril","ravenclaw undead"},["q"]="Who controls Beren's Peril?"},{["a"]="Forsaken scouts discovered that the undead holed up inside Beren's Peril were amassing troops and arming for an impending assault on the Sepulcher, prompting Shadow Priest Allister to order preemptive strikes against them.",["al"]={"allister berens peril","why attack berens peril","sepulcher threat"},["q"]="Why do the Forsaken care about this location?"},{["a"]="Thule Ravenclaw is a powerful necromancer operating in Silverpine Forest who maintained control over pockets of mindless and hostile Scourge minions, using sites like Beren's Peril and Fenris Keep to menace the region.",["al"]={"thule ravenclaw","thule silverpine"},["q"]="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?"}},["kw"]={"allister","ambermill","beren's peril","berens peril","ravenclaw drudge","scourge","sepulcher","silverpine","thule ravenclaw"},["n"]="Beren's Peril",["s"]="Beren's Peril is a secluded mountain cavern tucked in the rocky hills southwest of Ambermill in Silverpine Forest. It serves as an entrenched redoubt for rogue Scourge loyalists serving the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, plotting against the nearby Forsaken.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away high in the crags southwest of Ambermill, Beren's Peril consists of a shadowed cave and winding mountain path hidden from the main roadway. Following the devastation of the Third War, rogue Scourge undead under the command of the renegade necromancer Thule Ravenclaw fortified this enclave. Rather than bowing to the Dark Lady or retreating north, Ravenclaw's thralls—regents, guardians, and drudgers—gathered here in secret to muster an assault against the Forsaken base at the Sepulcher. Their presence was uncovered by Forsaken scouts, turning the quiet cliffside into an active warzone for Horde operatives sent to eliminate the threat before an attack could materialize.",["t"]="A Hidden Threat in the Hills"}}}}}
